WEBVTT


00:01:23.847 --> 00:01:25.747
Shit!


00:01:48.905 --> 00:01:50.270
Andrew, hey.


00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:54.767
Here you go.
Your regular lattes.


00:01:54.811 --> 00:01:59.009
Literally saved my life.
Thank you. Thank you.


00:02:13.663 --> 00:02:14.721
- Everyone OK?
- Yeah.


00:02:14.764 --> 00:02:17.028
- Yeah.
- Me too.


00:02:18.468 --> 00:02:21.767
Hello, Frank? How's my favorite writer?


00:02:21.805 --> 00:02:23.466
Of course you've been
thinking about our talk


00:02:23.506 --> 00:02:25.167
because you know I'm right.


00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:27.108
Frank, people in this
country are busy, broke,


00:02:27.143 --> 00:02:29.236
and they hate to read.
They need someone they can trust to say,


00:02:29.279 --> 00:02:31.611
"Hey! Don't watch
<i>CSl: Indianapolis</i> tonight.


00:02:31.648 --> 00:02:35.049
Read a book! Read Frank's book."
And that person is Oprah.


00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.119
- Cuttin' it close.
- One of those mornings.


00:02:42.158 --> 00:02:43.648
Thank you, Captain Obvious.


00:02:43.693 --> 00:02:45.957
Sweet...


00:02:45.996 --> 00:02:47.657
- Uh, sorry.
...Jesus!


00:02:47.697 --> 00:02:49.597
Rub some dirt on it, brother.


00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:53.091
Frank, the truth is all
A-plus novelists do publicity.


00:02:54.037 --> 00:02:56.835
Roth, McCourt, Russo, and...


00:02:56.873 --> 00:02:59.774
Frank! Can I tell you what else
they have in common? A Pulitzer.


00:03:00.477 --> 00:03:02.411
I need the shirt off
your back. Literally.


00:03:02.445 --> 00:03:05.903
- You're kidding, right?
- Yankees, Boston, this Tuesday,


00:03:05.949 --> 00:03:08.349
two company seats for your shirt.
You have five seconds to decide.


00:03:08.385 --> 00:03:10.046
Five, four, three, two, one.


00:03:10.086 --> 00:03:11.576
I know...


00:03:11.621 --> 00:03:13.885
- Shh!
- Later.


00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:20.960
Uh-oh.


00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:30.830
Uh, hello. Hello?


00:03:37.547 --> 00:03:39.447
Morning, boss. You have a
conference call in 30 minutes.


00:03:39.482 --> 00:03:41.450
Yes. About the marketing
of the spring books. I know.


00:03:41.484 --> 00:03:42.849
Staff meeting at 9:00.


00:03:42.886 --> 00:03:44.444
Did you call, um...
What's her name?


00:03:44.487 --> 00:03:46.921
The one with the ugly hands.


00:03:46.956 --> 00:03:47.980
- Janet.
- Yes, Janet.


00:03:48.024 --> 00:03:49.423
Yes. I did call her. I told her that


00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:51.154
if she doesn't get her
manuscript in on time


00:03:51.194 --> 00:03:53.594
you won't give her a release date.
Your immigration lawyer called.


00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:54.756
He said it's imperative...


00:03:54.798 --> 00:03:56.459
Cancel the call, push
the meeting to tomorrow


00:03:56.499 --> 00:03:57.932
and keep the lawyer on the sheets.


00:03:57.967 --> 00:03:59.434
Oh, and get a hold of PR,


00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:00.902
have them start drafting
a press release.


00:04:00.937 --> 00:04:02.404
Frank is doing <i>Oprah.</i>


00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:04.964
Wow. Nicely done.


00:04:05.008 --> 00:04:08.205
If I want your praise,
I will ask for it.


00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.214
Um...


00:04:12.248 --> 00:04:13.909
Who is, uh, who is Jillian?


00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.646
And why does she want me to call her?


00:04:19.856 --> 00:04:21.790
Well, that was originally my cup.


00:04:21.825 --> 00:04:23.793
And I'm drinking your coffee why?


00:04:23.827 --> 00:04:25.852
Because your coffee spilled.


00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:35.368
So, you drink unsweetened
cinnamon light soy lattes?


00:04:35.405 --> 00:04:38.465
I do. It's like Christmas in a cup.


00:04:38.508 --> 00:04:39.941
Is that a coincidence?


00:04:39.976 --> 00:04:42.376
Incredibly, it is.


00:04:42.412 --> 00:04:44.573
I mean I wouldn't possibly drink
the same coffee that you drink


00:04:44.614 --> 00:04:46.241
just in case yours spilled.


00:04:46.282 --> 00:04:48.079
That would be pathetic.


00:04:48.118 --> 00:04:50.143
Morning. Miss Tate's office.


00:04:50.186 --> 00:04:51.483
Hey, Bob.


00:04:53.156 --> 00:04:56.387
Actually, we're headed to
your office right now. Yeah.


00:04:56.426 --> 00:04:59.190
Why are we headed to Bob's office?


00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.698
Oop!


00:05:15.111 --> 00:05:16.703
Have you finished the
manuscript I gave you?


00:05:16.746 --> 00:05:19.306
Uh, I read a few pages.
I wasn't that impressed.


00:05:19.349 --> 00:05:20.714
- Can I say something?
- No.


00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.809
I've read thousands of manuscripts,


00:05:22.852 --> 00:05:24.251
and this is the only one
I've given you.


00:05:24.287 --> 00:05:26.016
There's an incredible novel in there.


00:05:26.055 --> 00:05:27.955
The kind of novel you used to publish.


00:05:27.991 --> 00:05:31.290
Uh, wrong. And I do think you
order the same coffee as I do


00:05:31.327 --> 00:05:33.818
just in case you spill,
which is, in fact, pathetic.


00:05:33.863 --> 00:05:35.125
- Or impressive.
- I'd be impressed


00:05:35.165 --> 00:05:36.393
if you didn't spill in the first place.


00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:37.866
Now remember, you're
just a prop in here.


00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:39.869
Won't say a word.


00:05:42.338 --> 00:05:47.275
Ah! Our fearless leader and
her liege. Please, do come in.


00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.939
Oh. Beautiful breakfront. Is it new?


00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:54.006
It is English Regency Egyptian
Revival, built in the 1800s


00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:56.883
but, yes, it is new to my office.


00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.547
Witty.


00:05:58.588 --> 00:06:01.216
Bob, I'm letting you go.


00:06:04.828 --> 00:06:05.852
Pardon?


00:06:05.895 --> 00:06:08.989
I asked you over a dozen times to get
Frank to do <i>Oprah,</i> and you didn't do it.


00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:11.125
You're fired.


00:06:13.002 --> 00:06:14.697
I have told you that is impossible.


00:06:14.737 --> 00:06:17.137
Frank hasn't done an
interview in 20 years.


00:06:17.173 --> 00:06:18.868
Well that is
interesting, because I just


00:06:18.908 --> 00:06:21.399
got off the phone
with him, and he is in.


00:06:22.679 --> 00:06:24.078
Excuse me?


00:06:24.113 --> 00:06:25.512
You didn't even call him, did you?


00:06:26.916 --> 00:06:28.645
- But...
- I know, I know.


00:06:28.685 --> 00:06:31.916
Frank can be a little scary
to deal with. For you.


00:06:31.955 --> 00:06:35.186
Now, I will give you two
months to find another job.


00:06:35.225 --> 00:06:37.693
And then you can tell
everyone you resigned, OK?


00:06:41.764 --> 00:06:43.857
What's his twenty?


00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:47.563
He's moving. He has crazy eyes.


00:06:47.604 --> 00:06:49.697
Don't do it, Bob. Don't do it.


00:06:49.739 --> 00:06:53.732
You poisonous bitch!


00:06:53.776 --> 00:06:55.437
You can't fire me!


00:06:55.478 --> 00:06:57.776
You don't think I see
what you're doing here?


00:06:57.814 --> 00:06:59.577
Sandbagging me on this Oprah thing


00:06:59.616 --> 00:07:01.516
just so that you can
look good to the board?


00:07:01.551 --> 00:07:04.543
Because you are threatened by me!


00:07:04.587 --> 00:07:07.454
- And you are a monster.
- Bob, stop.


00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:10.789
Just because you have
no semblance of a life


00:07:10.827 --> 00:07:12.590
outside of this office,


00:07:12.629 --> 00:07:14.756
you think that you can treat all of us


00:07:14.797 --> 00:07:16.458
like your own personal slaves.


00:07:16.499 --> 00:07:19.059
You know what? I feel sorry for you.


00:07:19.102 --> 00:07:21.832
Because you know what you're
gonna have on your deathbed?


00:07:21.871 --> 00:07:23.896
Nothing and no one.


00:07:28.745 --> 00:07:30.303
Listen carefully, Bob.


00:07:30.346 --> 00:07:33.941
I didn't fire you because
I feel threatened. No.


00:07:33.983 --> 00:07:37.384
I fired you because you're
lazy, entitled, incompetent


00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.081
and you spend more time
cheating on your wife


00:07:39.122 --> 00:07:40.453
than you do in your office.


00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:41.821
And if you say another word,


00:07:41.858 --> 00:07:44.156
Andrew here is gonna have you
thrown out on your ass, OK?


00:07:44.193 --> 00:07:46.718
Another word and you're
going out of here


00:07:46.763 --> 00:07:48.025
with an armed escort.


00:07:48.064 --> 00:07:49.929
Andrew will film it with
his little camera phone


00:07:49.966 --> 00:07:51.593
and he will put it
on that Internet site.


00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:52.862
- What was it?
- YouTube?


00:07:52.902 --> 00:07:55.336
Exactly. Is that what you want?


00:07:55.371 --> 00:07:56.998
Didn't think so. I have work to do.


00:07:59.342 --> 00:08:01.367
Have security take his
breakfront out of his office


00:08:01.411 --> 00:08:02.537
and put it in my conference room.


00:08:02.579 --> 00:08:03.603
Will do.


00:08:03.646 --> 00:08:04.738
And I need you around this weekend


00:08:04.781 --> 00:08:06.146
to help review his files
and his manuscript.


00:08:06.182 --> 00:08:08.776
- This weekend?
- You have a problem with that?


00:08:08.818 --> 00:08:10.843
No. I... just my
grandmother's 90th birthday,


00:08:10.887 --> 00:08:12.286
so I was gonna go home and...


00:08:12.322 --> 00:08:14.119
...it's fine. I'll cancel it.


00:08:14.157 --> 00:08:16.091
You're actually saving me from
a weekend of misery anyway,


00:08:16.125 --> 00:08:18.423
so it's... good talk, yeah.


00:08:18.461 --> 00:08:23.558
I know, I know. OK, tell
Gammy I'm sorry. OK? What...


00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.158
Mom. What do you want me to tell you?


00:08:25.201 --> 00:08:27.635
She's making me work the weekend.


00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:28.967
No, I'm not... no.


00:08:29.005 --> 00:08:30.563
Listen, I've worked too
hard for this promotion


00:08:30.607 --> 00:08:31.699
to throw it all away, OK?


00:08:31.741 --> 00:08:33.231
I'm sure that Dad is pissed,


00:08:33.276 --> 00:08:36.177
but we take all of our submissions
around here very seriously.


00:08:36.212 --> 00:08:39.613
We'll get back to
you as soon as we can.


00:08:39.649 --> 00:08:41.640
- Was that your family?
- Yes.


00:08:41.684 --> 00:08:43.413
- They tell you to quit?
- Every single day.


00:08:43.453 --> 00:08:46.650
Miss Tate's office.


00:08:46.689 --> 00:08:49.385
Oh... Yeah. OK. All right.


00:08:49.425 --> 00:08:51.518
Bergen and Malloy want to
see you upstairs immediately.


00:08:51.561 --> 00:08:54.155
OK. Come get me in ten
minutes. We've got a lot to do.


00:08:54.197 --> 00:08:55.221
Okey-doke.


00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:02.565
Good morning, Miss Tate.


00:09:04.774 --> 00:09:06.799
Jack, Edwin.


00:09:06.843 --> 00:09:08.606
Margaret, congratulations
on the <i>Oprah</i> thing.


00:09:08.645 --> 00:09:10.510
- That's terrific news.
- Thank you, thank you.


00:09:10.546 --> 00:09:13.413
This isn't about my second raise, is it?
Just kidding.


00:09:13.449 --> 00:09:17.078
Margaret, do you
remember when we agreed


00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.145
that you wouldn't go to
the Frankfurt Book Fair


00:09:19.188 --> 00:09:20.587
because you weren't allowed
out of the country


00:09:20.623 --> 00:09:22.523
while your visa application
was being processed?


00:09:22.558 --> 00:09:23.582
Yes. I do.


00:09:23.626 --> 00:09:25.992
And... you went to Frankfurt.


00:09:26.029 --> 00:09:28.224
Yes, I did. We were going
to lose DeLillo to Viking.


00:09:28.264 --> 00:09:30.289
So... really didn't
have a choice, did I?


00:09:30.333 --> 00:09:31.698
It seems that the
United States Government


00:09:31.734 --> 00:09:33.759
doesn't care much who
publishes Don DeLillo.


00:09:33.803 --> 00:09:36.567
We, uh, just spoke to
your immigration attorney.


00:09:36.606 --> 00:09:39.234
Great. So, we're all good?
Everything good?


00:09:39.275 --> 00:09:41.743
Margaret, your visa application
has been denied.


00:09:41.778 --> 00:09:44.941
And you are being deported.


00:09:44.981 --> 00:09:46.107
Deported?


00:09:46.149 --> 00:09:47.844
And apparently there
was also some paperwork


00:09:47.884 --> 00:09:49.249
that you didn't fill out in time.


00:09:49.285 --> 00:09:53.745
Come on. Come on! It's not
like I'm even an immigrant!


00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:55.781
I'm from Canada, for Christ's sake.


00:09:55.825 --> 00:09:58.191
There's gotta be... there's
gotta be something we can do.


00:09:58.227 --> 00:10:00.195
We can reapply, but unfortunately


00:10:00.229 --> 00:10:03.221
you have to leave the country
for at least a year.


00:10:05.268 --> 00:10:10.171
OK. OK, well, that's
not ideal, but, uh...,


00:10:10.206 --> 00:10:12.003
I can, uh... I can manage
everything from Toronto...


00:10:12.041 --> 00:10:13.201
No, Margaret.


00:10:13.242 --> 00:10:14.539
...with videoconferencing
and Internet.


00:10:14.577 --> 00:10:15.703
Unfortunately, Margaret,


00:10:15.745 --> 00:10:18.441
if you're deported,
you can't work for an American company.


00:10:18.481 --> 00:10:20.881
Until this is resolved I'm going
to turn operations over


00:10:20.917 --> 00:10:22.111
to Bob Spaulding.


00:10:22.151 --> 00:10:24.813
Bob Spaulding? The guy I just fired?


00:10:24.854 --> 00:10:26.253
We need an editor in chief.


00:10:26.289 --> 00:10:28.655
He is the only person in the building
who has enough experience.


00:10:28.691 --> 00:10:30.522
- You cannot be serious. I beg of you.
- Margaret.


00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:32.528
We are desperate to have you stay.


00:10:32.562 --> 00:10:35.531
If there was any way, any way at all


00:10:35.565 --> 00:10:37.123
that we could make this work,
we'd be doing it.


00:10:37.166 --> 00:10:38.292
There is no way...


00:10:38.334 --> 00:10:39.358
I am begging you.


00:10:39.402 --> 00:10:41.029
No, Margaret. Excuse me,
we're in a meeting.


00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.628
- Sorry to interrupt.
- What? What!


00:10:42.672 --> 00:10:45.232
Mary from Miss Winfrey's office
called. She's on the line.


00:10:45.274 --> 00:10:46.332
- I know.
- She's on hold.


00:10:46.375 --> 00:10:49.310
She needs to speak with you right away.
I told her you were otherwise engaged.


00:10:49.345 --> 00:10:51.905
She insisted, so... sorry.


00:10:51.948 --> 00:10:53.575
So...


00:11:03.559 --> 00:11:05.584
Uh...


00:11:06.763 --> 00:11:08.230
Come here.


00:11:10.666 --> 00:11:14.432
Uh... Gentlemen, I understand.
I understand...


00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:17.564
the predicament that we are in.


00:11:17.607 --> 00:11:19.268
And, um...


00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.374
And there's, uh... well...


00:11:23.412 --> 00:11:26.040
I think there's something
that you should know.


00:11:27.383 --> 00:11:30.784
Uh... we're, uh...
we're getting married.


00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.913
We are getting married.


00:11:32.955 --> 00:11:34.582
- Who is getting married?
- You and I.


00:11:34.624 --> 00:11:37.388
You and I are getting married! Yes.


00:11:37.426 --> 00:11:39.087
- We are.
- Getting married.


00:11:39.128 --> 00:11:40.561
- We are getting married.
- Yes.


00:11:42.331 --> 00:11:44.424
Isn't he your secretary?


00:11:44.467 --> 00:11:45.525
Assistant.


00:11:45.568 --> 00:11:49.299
Executive, uh...
assistant secretary. Titles.


00:11:49.338 --> 00:11:53.604
But, wouldn't be the first time
one of us fell for our secretaries.


00:11:53.643 --> 00:11:55.634
Would it, Edwin?


00:11:55.678 --> 00:11:57.908
With Laquisha. Remember?


00:11:57.947 --> 00:12:01.474
So, yeah... The truth is,


00:12:01.517 --> 00:12:05.647
you know, Andrew and I, we're...
we are just two people


00:12:05.688 --> 00:12:07.849
who weren't meant to
fall in love but we did.


00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.221
No.


00:12:09.258 --> 00:12:14.286
All those late nights at the
office and weekend book fairs.


00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.388
- Yeah...
- No.


00:12:15.431 --> 00:12:18.093
- Something happened.
- Something.


00:12:18.134 --> 00:12:21.262
Yeah. Tried to fight it and...


00:12:21.304 --> 00:12:22.931
Can't, can't fight a...


00:12:22.972 --> 00:12:27.432
Can't fight a love like ours, so, uh...


00:12:27.476 --> 00:12:30.877
Uh... Are we good with this?
Are you happy?


00:12:30.913 --> 00:12:34.781
Because, well... we are happy. So happy.


00:12:34.817 --> 00:12:35.943
- Margaret.
- Yes?


00:12:35.985 --> 00:12:37.885
It's terrific.


00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.649
Just make it legal. Mmm?


00:12:39.689 --> 00:12:42.317
Oh! Legal.


00:12:42.358 --> 00:12:45.691
Yeah, well, then...
then that means we...


00:12:45.728 --> 00:12:48.026
...we need to get ourselves
to the immigration office.


00:12:48.064 --> 00:12:50.692
So we can work this
whole mess out. Right?


00:12:50.733 --> 00:12:52.598
Thank you
very much, gentlemen.


00:12:52.635 --> 00:12:53.693
We will do that right away.


00:12:53.736 --> 00:12:55.931
Thank you very much,
gentlemen. Thank you.


00:12:55.972 --> 00:12:58.202
- Gentlemen.
- Thank you.


00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.878
Margaret
and Andrew are getting married!


00:13:02.912 --> 00:13:04.209
What is that about?


00:13:04.247 --> 00:13:06.306
Dragon Lady!
Here they come...


00:13:06.349 --> 00:13:07.680
Yeah.


00:13:07.717 --> 00:13:09.480
What is he thinking?


00:13:09.518 --> 00:13:10.610
Mmm-mmm-mmm.


00:13:12.722 --> 00:13:15.316
Dude, for real. Her?


00:13:15.358 --> 00:13:17.622
Married? Didn't
even know they were dating...


00:13:39.582 --> 00:13:40.606
What?


00:13:41.984 --> 00:13:43.884
I don't understand what's happening.


00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.888
Relax. This is for you, too.


00:13:45.922 --> 00:13:47.253
Do explain.


00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:49.520
They were going to make Bob chief.


00:13:49.558 --> 00:13:51.219
So naturally I would have to marry you.


00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.852
And what's the problem?


00:13:52.895 --> 00:13:55.227
Like you were saving yourself
for someone special?


00:13:55.264 --> 00:13:58.392
I like to think so.
Besides, it's illegal.


00:13:58.434 --> 00:14:01.631
They're looking for terrorists,
not for book publishers.


00:14:01.671 --> 00:14:03.195
- Margaret.
- Yes?


00:14:03.239 --> 00:14:06.299
- I'm not gonna marry you.
- Sure you are.


00:14:06.342 --> 00:14:09.368
Because if you don't marry me, your
dreams of touching the lives of millions


00:14:09.412 --> 00:14:11.141
with the written word are dead.


00:14:17.086 --> 00:14:19.611
Bob is gonna fire you the second
I'm gone. Guaranteed.


00:14:19.655 --> 00:14:21.714
That means you're out on the street
alone looking for a job.


00:14:21.757 --> 00:14:24.248
That means all the time that
we spent together, all the lattes,


00:14:24.293 --> 00:14:26.488
all the canceled dates,
all the midnight Tampax runs,


00:14:26.529 --> 00:14:29.828
were all for nothing and all your dreams
of being an editor are gone.


00:14:29.865 --> 00:14:32.265
But don't worry, after the required
allotment of time,


00:14:32.301 --> 00:14:33.768
we'll get a quickie divorce
and you'll be done with me.


00:14:33.803 --> 00:14:35.634
But until then, like it or not,


00:14:35.671 --> 00:14:37.605
your wagon is hitched to mine. OK?


00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.835
Phone.


00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.751
- This way.
- Margaret.


00:14:55.791 --> 00:14:57.816
- Come.
- The line...


00:14:57.860 --> 00:14:58.884
Next, please.


00:14:58.928 --> 00:15:00.555
Ooh, ooh. Just, uh...


00:15:00.596 --> 00:15:02.120
Sorry, I just need to ask him something.


00:15:02.164 --> 00:15:04.962
I need for you to file this
fiancée visa for me, please.


00:15:09.605 --> 00:15:12.005
- Miss Tate?
- Yes.


00:15:12.041 --> 00:15:14.100
Please, come with me.


00:15:14.143 --> 00:15:16.703
Yes, ma'am, I understand
that. We're backed up...


00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.110
I have a bad feeling about this.


00:15:23.786 --> 00:15:25.151
- Hi. Hello.
- Hello.


00:15:25.187 --> 00:15:27.678
Hi. I'm Mr. Gilbertson.


00:15:27.723 --> 00:15:29.782
- Ah!
- And you must be Andrew,


00:15:29.825 --> 00:15:31.156
- and you must be...
- Margaret.


00:15:31.193 --> 00:15:32.990
...Margaret. Sorry about the wait.


00:15:33.029 --> 00:15:34.690
It's a, uh, crazy day today.


00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:36.891
Oh, of course, of course. We understand.


00:15:36.932 --> 00:15:38.957
And I can't tell you how much
we appreciate you seeing us


00:15:39.001 --> 00:15:43.062
- on such short notice.
- OK.


00:15:43.105 --> 00:15:45.596
<i># Buh, buh, buh, buh, buh</i>
<i>buh, buh, buh, buuuh</i>


00:15:45.641 --> 00:15:47.472
So, I have one question for you.


00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:50.707
Are you both committing fraud
to avoid her deportation


00:15:50.746 --> 00:15:54.842
so she can keep her position
as editor in chief at Colden Books?


00:15:56.419 --> 00:15:58.512
- That's ridiculous.
- Where did you hear that?


00:15:58.554 --> 00:16:00.852
We had a phone tip this afternoon
from a man named...


00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.653
Would it be Bob Spaulding?


00:16:02.691 --> 00:16:04.022
Bob Spaulding.


00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:07.359
Bob. Poor Bob. I am so sorry.


00:16:07.396 --> 00:16:11.332
Bob is nothing but a disgruntled
former employee.


00:16:11.367 --> 00:16:12.459
And I apologize.


00:16:12.501 --> 00:16:15.197
But we know you're incredibly busy


00:16:15.237 --> 00:16:19.105
with a room full of gardeners
and delivery boys to tend to.


00:16:19.141 --> 00:16:20.699
If you just give us our next step,


00:16:20.743 --> 00:16:22.768
we will be out of your
hair and on our way.


00:16:23.879 --> 00:16:25.437
Miss Tate, please.


00:16:26.849 --> 00:16:30.979
Let me explain to you the
process that's about to unfold.


00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:34.421
Step one will be a scheduled interview.


00:16:34.457 --> 00:16:37.984
I'll put you each in a room,
and I'll ask you every little question


00:16:38.027 --> 00:16:39.995
that a real couple
would know about each other.


00:16:40.029 --> 00:16:44.227
Step two, I dig deeper.
I look at your phone records,


00:16:44.266 --> 00:16:46.598
I talk to your neighbors,
I interview your coworkers.


00:16:46.635 --> 00:16:49.069
If your answers don't match up
at every point,


00:16:49.105 --> 00:16:51.767
you will be deported indefinitely.


00:16:51.807 --> 00:16:54.207
And you, young man,
will have committed a felony...


00:16:54.243 --> 00:16:58.236
...punishable by a fine of $250,000


00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.512
and a stay of five years
in federal prison.


00:17:05.621 --> 00:17:08.852
So, Andrew.


00:17:08.891 --> 00:17:12.292
You wanna... you want to talk to me?


00:17:16.132 --> 00:17:17.929
No?


00:17:20.469 --> 00:17:21.902
Yes?


00:17:26.008 --> 00:17:27.873
The truth is...


00:17:30.946 --> 00:17:35.713
Mr. Gilbertson, the truth is...


00:17:35.751 --> 00:17:37.514
Margaret and I...


00:17:40.289 --> 00:17:42.257
...are just two people


00:17:42.291 --> 00:17:45.283
who weren't supposed to fall in love.


00:17:46.162 --> 00:17:47.857
But did.


00:17:49.665 --> 00:17:51.895
We couldn't tell anyone we work with


00:17:51.934 --> 00:17:54.528
because of my big promotion
that I had coming up.


00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.037
- Promotion?
- Yeah.


00:17:56.071 --> 00:17:59.905
- Your?
- We... we both felt, uh...


00:17:59.942 --> 00:18:04.072
...that it would be deeply inappropriate
if I were to be promoted to editor.


00:18:04.113 --> 00:18:06.775
- Editor. Mmm-hmm.
...while we were...


00:18:08.284 --> 00:18:10.844
So...


00:18:10.886 --> 00:18:13.946
Have the two of you told your parents
about your secret love?


00:18:13.989 --> 00:18:17.322
Oh, I... impossible.
My parents are dead.


00:18:17.359 --> 00:18:19.623
- No brothers or sisters either.
- Gone.


00:18:19.662 --> 00:18:21.960
Are your parents dead?


00:18:21.997 --> 00:18:24.158
- Oh, no, his are very much alive.
- No... very much.


00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.499
Very much. They're, ah... Well,
we were gonna tell them this weekend.


00:18:27.536 --> 00:18:31.495
Gammy's 90th birthday, and the whole
family's coming together.


00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.132
And we thought it'd be a nice surprise.


00:18:33.175 --> 00:18:35.200
And where is this
surprise gonna take place?


00:18:35.244 --> 00:18:37.337
At Andrew's parents' house.


00:18:37.379 --> 00:18:38.505
Where is that located again?


00:18:38.547 --> 00:18:41.175
Um...
Why am I doing all the talking?


00:18:41.217 --> 00:18:42.582
It's your parents' house.


00:18:42.618 --> 00:18:44.051
Why don't you tell him
where it is. Jump in.


00:18:45.487 --> 00:18:48.217
- Sitka.
- Sitka.


00:18:48.257 --> 00:18:50.282
- Alaska.
- Alaska?


00:18:50.326 --> 00:18:52.419
You're gonna go to Alaska this weekend?


00:18:53.963 --> 00:18:55.931
- Yeah.
- Yes, yes.


00:18:55.965 --> 00:18:59.162
We are going to Alaska.
Alaska, that's where...


00:18:59.201 --> 00:19:02.102
That's where my little...
that's where my Andrew's from.


00:19:03.639 --> 00:19:04.970
OK.


00:19:05.007 --> 00:19:08.465
Fine. I see how this is gonna go.


00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:11.445
I will see you both
at 11:00 Monday morning


00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:13.448
for your scheduled interview,


00:19:13.482 --> 00:19:16.883
and your answers better
match up on every account.


00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:19.485
- Thank you.
- Hello?


00:19:19.521 --> 00:19:21.614
- I'm looking forward to this one.
- We're looking forward to this one.


00:19:21.657 --> 00:19:22.715
Thank you.


00:19:22.758 --> 00:19:25.522
Gonna be fun.
I'll be checking up on you.


00:19:25.561 --> 00:19:26.585
You got it.


00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:36.000
OK... so, what's gonna happen is
we will go up there.


00:19:36.038 --> 00:19:38.063
We will pretend like we're
boyfriend and girlfriend,


00:19:38.107 --> 00:19:39.699
tell your parents we're engaged.


00:19:39.742 --> 00:19:41.334
Uh, use the miles for the tickets.


00:19:41.377 --> 00:19:45.074
I guess I will pop for you to fly first
class. But make sure you use the miles.


00:19:45.114 --> 00:19:46.445
If we don't get the miles,
we're not doing it.


00:19:46.482 --> 00:19:48.416
Oh, and please confirm
the vegan meal, OK?


00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:50.418
'Cause last time they actually
gave it to a vegan,


00:19:50.452 --> 00:19:52.079
and they, uh... forced me to eat


00:19:52.121 --> 00:19:54.612
this clammy, warm, creamy
salad thing, which was...


00:19:54.657 --> 00:19:56.648
Hey, I'm... Why aren't you taking notes?


00:19:56.692 --> 00:19:59.024
I'm sorry, were you not in that room?


00:19:59.061 --> 00:20:00.426
What? What?


00:20:01.797 --> 00:20:04.288
Oh! The thing you said about
being promoted?


00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:06.324
Genius! Genius.
He completely fell for it.


00:20:06.368 --> 00:20:07.630
I was serious.


00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:10.571
I'm looking at a $250,000 fine
and five years in jail.


00:20:10.606 --> 00:20:11.800
That changes things.


00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.970
- Promote you to editor? No, no way.
- Then I quit, and you're screwed.


00:20:16.011 --> 00:20:17.035
Bye-bye, Margaret.


00:20:17.079 --> 00:20:18.546
- Andrew!
- It really has been


00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.981
- a little slice of heaven.
- Andrew, Andrew! Fine, fine.


00:20:23.319 --> 00:20:25.253
I'll make you editor. Fine.


00:20:25.287 --> 00:20:28.882
If you do the Alaska weekend
and the immigration interview,


00:20:28.924 --> 00:20:31.825
I will make you editor. Happy?


00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.260
- And not in two years. Right away.
- Fine.


00:20:34.296 --> 00:20:35.786
And you'll publish my manuscript.


00:20:37.633 --> 00:20:38.998
Ten thousand copy first...


00:20:39.034 --> 00:20:40.592
Twenty thousand copies, first run.


00:20:40.636 --> 00:20:42.570
And we'll tell my family
about our engagement


00:20:42.604 --> 00:20:44.231
when I want and how I want.


00:20:44.273 --> 00:20:46.571
Now, ask me nicely.


00:20:46.608 --> 00:20:47.768
"Ask you nicely" what?


00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:51.576
Ask me nicely to marry you, Margaret.


00:20:53.615 --> 00:20:56.641
- What does that mean?
- You heard me. On your knee.


00:21:05.794 --> 00:21:06.818
Fine.


00:21:15.237 --> 00:21:17.569
- Does this work for you?
- Oh, I like this. Yeah.


00:21:17.606 --> 00:21:19.767
- Will you marry me?
- No.


00:21:19.808 --> 00:21:21.366
Say it like you mean it.


00:21:24.513 --> 00:21:27.380
- Andrew?
- Yes, Margaret?


00:21:27.416 --> 00:21:30.510
- Sweet Andrew?
- I'm listening.


00:21:30.552 --> 00:21:33.544
Would you please,
with cherries on top, marry me?


00:21:36.158 --> 00:21:38.820
OK. I don't appreciate the sarcasm,
but I'll do it.


00:21:38.861 --> 00:21:41.489
- See you at the airport tomorrow.
- Good.


00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:57.902
So, these are the questions
that INS is gonna ask us.


00:21:57.946 --> 00:22:00.938
Now, the good news is is
I know everything about you,


00:22:00.983 --> 00:22:02.678
but the bad news is
that you have four days


00:22:02.718 --> 00:22:07.519
to learn all this about me.
So, you should... probably get studying.


00:22:11.093 --> 00:22:13.357
You know all the answers
to these questions about me?


00:22:13.395 --> 00:22:15.420
- Scary, isn't it?
- A little bit.


00:22:15.464 --> 00:22:17.864
- What am I allergic to?
- Pine nuts.


00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:19.834
And the full spectrum of human emotion.


00:22:19.868 --> 00:22:21.836
Oh, that's... that was funny.


00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:23.667
- Mmm-hmm.
- Umm...


00:22:23.705 --> 00:22:26.572
Here's a good one. Do I have any scars?


00:22:26.608 --> 00:22:28.508
I'm pretty sure that you have a tattoo.


00:22:28.544 --> 00:22:30.205
Oh, you're pretty sure?


00:22:30.245 --> 00:22:32.611
I'm pretty sure. Two years ago,
your dermatologist called


00:22:32.648 --> 00:22:34.582
and asked about a Q-switched laser.


00:22:34.616 --> 00:22:36.174
I of course Googled a Q-switched laser


00:22:36.218 --> 00:22:38.516
and found that they
in fact do remove tattoos.


00:22:38.554 --> 00:22:40.112
But you canceled your appointment.


00:22:41.690 --> 00:22:43.248
So what is it? Tribal ink?


00:22:43.292 --> 00:22:45.226
Japanese calligraphy? Barbed wire?


00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:48.093
You know, it's exciting for me
to experience you like this.


00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.394
Thank you. You're gonna have
to tell me where it is, though.


00:22:50.432 --> 00:22:51.899
- No, I'm not.
- They're gonna ask.


00:22:51.934 --> 00:22:54.459
We're done with that question.
We're done with that question.


00:22:54.503 --> 00:22:56.698
On to another question.
Let me see, let me see.


00:22:56.738 --> 00:22:59.605
Oh, here's one. Whose place do we
stay at, yours or mine?


00:22:59.641 --> 00:23:01.040
That's easy. Mine.


00:23:01.076 --> 00:23:02.941
And why wouldn't we stay at mine?


00:23:02.978 --> 00:23:05.469
Because I live at Central Park West.


00:23:05.514 --> 00:23:08.449
And you probably live at some
squalid little studio apartment


00:23:08.484 --> 00:23:11.453
with stacks of yellowed
Penguin Classics.


00:23:11.487 --> 00:23:14.456
<i> Ladies and gentlemen,</i>
<i>please fasten your seat belts.</i>


00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:17.084
<i>We are beginning our descent</i>
<i>into Juneau.</i>


00:23:17.125 --> 00:23:18.854
Juneau? I thought
we were going to Sitka.


00:23:20.128 --> 00:23:24.155
- We are.
- How are we getting to Sitka?


00:23:28.237 --> 00:23:29.329
Whoa.


00:23:53.328 --> 00:23:56.593
All right. Here we go.


00:23:59.034 --> 00:24:00.968
- Oh, there he is!
- Andrew!


00:24:07.843 --> 00:24:09.504
Hi. Right this way...


00:24:13.081 --> 00:24:14.878
- Hi!
- Oh...


00:24:14.917 --> 00:24:17.511
- It's so good to see you!
- You're suffocating him, Grace.


00:24:17.553 --> 00:24:19.453
- Come here.
- Hey, Gammy.


00:24:19.488 --> 00:24:22.252
Ah, Gammy. How are you doing?
Where's Dad?


00:24:22.291 --> 00:24:24.987
Oh, you know your father.
He's always working.


00:24:25.027 --> 00:24:27.393
Never mind about him. Where's your girl?


00:24:27.429 --> 00:24:29.897
Uh, she's... right there.


00:24:29.932 --> 00:24:31.524
- Ah.
- There she is.


00:24:31.567 --> 00:24:34.536
I guess the word "girl"
is inappropriate.


00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:35.901
Annie.


00:24:37.005 --> 00:24:38.029
- Hi!
- Hello.


00:24:38.073 --> 00:24:39.836
- Margaret, this is my mom.
- Oh, hello.


00:24:39.875 --> 00:24:42.309
Yeah, great. This is my gammy, Annie.


00:24:42.344 --> 00:24:45.438
- Pleasure.
- Well, hello there.


00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:50.474
Now, do you prefer being called Margaret
or Satan's Mistress?


00:24:50.519 --> 00:24:52.384
We've heard it both ways.


00:24:52.421 --> 00:24:54.218
Actually we've heard it
lots of ways.


00:24:54.256 --> 00:24:55.848
She's kidding.


00:24:55.891 --> 00:24:58.359
Oh! Oh... OK.


00:24:58.393 --> 00:24:59.860
Thank you so much for...


00:24:59.895 --> 00:25:01.590
allowing me to be a part
of this weekend.


00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:04.827
Oh, you're welcome.
We're thrilled to have you.


00:25:04.866 --> 00:25:06.595
Let's get you two back to the fort.


00:25:06.635 --> 00:25:08.762
- OK.
- Oh...


00:25:08.804 --> 00:25:11.830
- It's so good to see you.
- There we are.


00:25:45.707 --> 00:25:46.969
Andrew...


00:25:47.009 --> 00:25:50.467
Andrew. Andrew!


00:25:52.347 --> 00:25:54.941
Please, don't do that.


00:25:54.983 --> 00:25:58.146
You didn't tell me about all
the family businesses, honey.


00:25:58.186 --> 00:26:01.383
He was probably just
being modest, dear.


00:26:01.423 --> 00:26:02.913
Oh.


00:26:10.365 --> 00:26:13.493
What are we doing? Shouldn't we
check into our hotel right now?


00:26:13.535 --> 00:26:15.935
Oh, we canceled your reservation.


00:26:15.971 --> 00:26:17.404
Family doesn't stay at a hotel.


00:26:17.439 --> 00:26:19.134
You're gonna stay in our home.


00:26:19.174 --> 00:26:21.165
Oh, great! Great.


00:26:21.209 --> 00:26:22.608
- What?
- God.


00:26:22.644 --> 00:26:24.839
You're gonna wanna use your legs
to lift that one.


00:26:24.880 --> 00:26:27.713
Andrew! Help her with those.


00:26:27.749 --> 00:26:30.240
I'd love to, but she won't let me
do anything.


00:26:30.285 --> 00:26:33.777
She insists on doing it all herself.
She's one of those... she's a feminist.


00:26:42.998 --> 00:26:44.226
Come on, sweetie.


00:26:45.701 --> 00:26:48.295
You see the shoes
that broad was wearing?


00:26:57.846 --> 00:26:58.972
This is the last of 'em.


00:27:00.549 --> 00:27:01.811
- Oh!
- Ooh.


00:27:01.850 --> 00:27:05.013
- Five second rule.
- Got it!


00:27:05.053 --> 00:27:07.385
That will dry right off.


00:27:07.422 --> 00:27:09.652
Psst! Psst!
I'm not getting on that boat.


00:27:09.691 --> 00:27:11.556
You don't have to.
See you in a few days.


00:27:11.593 --> 00:27:13.823
Psst! You know I can't swim.


00:27:13.862 --> 00:27:16.353
Hence, the boat.


00:27:23.338 --> 00:27:24.737
Come on.


00:27:29.244 --> 00:27:31.212
Come on. Here we go.


00:27:37.953 --> 00:27:41.184
Looking good, boss.
Take your time, though.


00:27:41.223 --> 00:27:43.282
Shh.


00:27:47.996 --> 00:27:50.191
She comes with a lot of baggage.


00:27:50.232 --> 00:27:51.563
Just gonna give you
a little hand here.


00:27:53.535 --> 00:27:56.470
Hand off ass! Off ass!


00:27:59.040 --> 00:28:02.134
There you go. You're there.


00:28:06.414 --> 00:28:10.441
Congratulations.
I'm a hundred years old now.


00:28:36.812 --> 00:28:38.939
Here we are. We're home.


00:28:41.283 --> 00:28:43.342
That is your home?


00:28:44.653 --> 00:28:46.780
Who are you people?


00:29:01.136 --> 00:29:02.660
Why did you tell me
you were poor?


00:29:02.704 --> 00:29:05.537
- I never said I was poor.
- But you never told me you were rich.


00:29:05.574 --> 00:29:07.769
I'm not rich. My parents are rich.


00:29:07.809 --> 00:29:10.243
OK, you know what?
That's something only rich people say.


00:29:10.278 --> 00:29:11.802
Hey, Andrew! Welcome home!


00:29:11.847 --> 00:29:14.577
Hi! Mom, what is this?


00:29:14.616 --> 00:29:17.244
Nothing. It's just a little
welcoming party.


00:29:17.285 --> 00:29:18.513
Is that a crime?


00:29:18.553 --> 00:29:20.680
Just 50 of our closest
friends and neighbors.


00:29:20.722 --> 00:29:22.383
And all excited to meet you.


00:29:22.424 --> 00:29:24.756
- Oh, good. Good.
- Come on. Come on.


00:29:24.793 --> 00:29:27.091
- A party?
- Yeah, I guess so.


00:29:27.128 --> 00:29:29.756
Come on. Let's go. My grandma's
moving faster than you.


00:29:31.366 --> 00:29:32.765
Put your back into it.


00:29:38.406 --> 00:29:40.601
So nice to meet you,
Margaret. Welcome to Sitka.


00:29:40.642 --> 00:29:42.633
Jill? Hi. Nice to meet you.
My pleasure.


00:29:42.677 --> 00:29:45.840
Why didn't you tell me you were
some kind of Alaskan Kennedy?


00:29:45.881 --> 00:29:46.939
How could I?


00:29:46.982 --> 00:29:50.474
We were in the middle of talking about
you for the last three years.


00:29:50.518 --> 00:29:52.213
OK, know what? Timeout, OK?


00:29:52.254 --> 00:29:53.983
This bickering Bickerson thing
has got to stop.


00:29:54.022 --> 00:29:56.013
People need to think that we are
in love. So let's just...


00:29:56.057 --> 00:29:57.581
That, that's no problem.
I can do that.


00:29:57.626 --> 00:30:00.493
I can pretend to be the doting fiancé.
That's easy.


00:30:00.528 --> 00:30:01.995
But for you, it's going to require


00:30:02.030 --> 00:30:04.430
that you stop snacking on
children while they dream.


00:30:04.466 --> 00:30:07.162
Very funny. When are you going
to tell them we're engaged?


00:30:07.202 --> 00:30:08.567
I'll pick the right moment.


00:30:08.603 --> 00:30:12.471
Hey, Andrew. Hi!


00:30:12.507 --> 00:30:15.135
Mrs. McKittrick. How are you?
Nice to see you.


00:30:15.176 --> 00:30:17.167
Nice to see you, Mr. McKittrick.
This is Margaret.


00:30:17.212 --> 00:30:19.077
- Hi. Pleasure.
- Margaret!


00:30:19.114 --> 00:30:20.513
Hi, how are you? Pleasure.


00:30:20.548 --> 00:30:23.949
So I always wanted to know,
what does a book editor do?


00:30:23.985 --> 00:30:26.078
That's a great question, Louise.


00:30:26.121 --> 00:30:28.521
I'm curious to know the answer myself.


00:30:29.624 --> 00:30:31.353
- Hello, Dad.
- Son.


00:30:32.160 --> 00:30:33.684
This must be Maggie.


00:30:33.728 --> 00:30:35.355
Uh, Margaret.


00:30:35.397 --> 00:30:38.855
- Joe. Pleasure to meet you.
- Pleasure's mine.


00:30:38.900 --> 00:30:42.495
So why don't you tell us exactly
what a book editor does.


00:30:42.537 --> 00:30:45.995
Besides taking writers out
to lunch and getting bombed.


00:30:46.041 --> 00:30:48.407
Now that sounds like fun.


00:30:48.443 --> 00:30:50.240
No wonder you like being an editor.


00:30:50.278 --> 00:30:53.509
No, Louise. Andrew's not an editor,
he's an editor's assistant.


00:30:53.548 --> 00:30:56.039
Maggie here is the editor.


00:30:56.084 --> 00:30:57.642
Margaret.


00:30:57.686 --> 00:31:01.178
- So you're actually...
- Andrew's boss. Yeah.


00:31:01.222 --> 00:31:02.849
Well. How about that.


00:31:02.891 --> 00:31:04.256
Huh.


00:31:04.292 --> 00:31:06.283
I think I'll get a refill.


00:31:08.463 --> 00:31:09.828
Charming.


00:31:13.635 --> 00:31:16.695
That's a hell of
a first impression, Dad.


00:31:16.738 --> 00:31:18.797
What the hell, Andrew?


00:31:18.840 --> 00:31:21.604
You show up here after all this
time with this woman you hated


00:31:21.643 --> 00:31:22.974
- and now she's your girlfriend?
- We just got here.


00:31:23.011 --> 00:31:24.308
Can we wait two seconds


00:31:24.346 --> 00:31:25.779
before we throw the
kitchen sink at each other?


00:31:25.814 --> 00:31:29.045
Just never figured you for a guy
who slept his way to the middle.


00:31:29.084 --> 00:31:30.779
Actually, I'll have you know
that that woman in there


00:31:30.819 --> 00:31:32.446
is one of the most
respected editors in town.


00:31:32.487 --> 00:31:33.579
She's your meal ticket,


00:31:33.621 --> 00:31:35.088
and you brought her home
to meet your mother.


00:31:35.123 --> 00:31:39.492
She's not my meal ticket, Dad.
She's my fiancée.


00:31:39.527 --> 00:31:42.087
- What'd you say?
- You heard me.


00:31:42.130 --> 00:31:43.927
I'm getting married.


00:31:47.502 --> 00:31:49.402
- How are you?
- Good, good. Thank you.


00:31:49.437 --> 00:31:50.768
Would you care for
some hors d'oeuvres?


00:31:50.805 --> 00:31:52.102
No, I'm fine. Thank you very much.


00:31:52.140 --> 00:31:53.471
It's a tradition.


00:31:53.508 --> 00:31:55.169
It's the texture. I'm not a fish person.


00:31:55.210 --> 00:31:57.610
- You'll like it.
- You're very sweet.


00:31:57.645 --> 00:32:00.239
I think if you'll just taste it.


00:32:00.281 --> 00:32:01.680
Thank you so much.


00:32:05.520 --> 00:32:06.646
Ladies and gentlemen...


00:32:06.688 --> 00:32:09.179
I have a very important
announcement to make.


00:32:09.224 --> 00:32:10.816
Margaret and I are getting married.


00:32:10.859 --> 00:32:12.121
It's the paprika.


00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:13.525
So sorry.


00:32:13.561 --> 00:32:16.359
That's OK. It's wash-and-wear.


00:32:18.199 --> 00:32:21.191
Yep. Honey? Where you at?


00:32:22.404 --> 00:32:23.701
Here it is.


00:32:26.674 --> 00:32:28.369
Come on down here, pumpkin.


00:32:28.410 --> 00:32:30.207
- All right.
- OK.


00:32:30.245 --> 00:32:32.805
Oh, look at her. Look at her.


00:32:34.049 --> 00:32:36.483
Right there, ladies and
gentlemen. There she is.


00:32:36.518 --> 00:32:38.952
Congratulations, Andrew.


00:32:38.987 --> 00:32:40.011
Thank you.


00:32:40.055 --> 00:32:41.920
Thank you very much.


00:32:41.956 --> 00:32:44.516
- Time to celebrate.
- Get the champagne.


00:32:47.495 --> 00:32:49.122
So that was your idea
of the perfect time


00:32:49.164 --> 00:32:50.358
- to tell them we're engaged?
- Mmm.


00:32:50.398 --> 00:32:52.059
'Cause it was brilliant.
Brilliant timing.


00:32:52.100 --> 00:32:54.068
Andrew. Hi.


00:32:54.102 --> 00:32:58.038
Gert? Oh, my God. Hey, hi. Wow.


00:32:58.073 --> 00:33:00.507
How you doing? I didn't know
that you were gonna be here.


00:33:00.542 --> 00:33:03.807
Your mom probably wanted it to
be a surprise. So... surprise.


00:33:03.845 --> 00:33:06.336
- Right.
- And...


00:33:06.381 --> 00:33:09.316
...we're being completely rude. Hi.


00:33:09.350 --> 00:33:12.547
- Oh, God. This is my ex...
- Hi. I'm Gertrude.


00:33:12.587 --> 00:33:15.021
- Oh! Oh, wow. Wow!
- You can call me Gert.


00:33:15.056 --> 00:33:17.251
Well, congratulations, you guys.


00:33:17.292 --> 00:33:18.725
- Thank you.
- Thank you.


00:33:18.760 --> 00:33:20.284
So did I miss the story?


00:33:21.096 --> 00:33:22.256
- What story?
- What story?


00:33:22.297 --> 00:33:24.060
About how you proposed.


00:33:24.099 --> 00:33:28.433
Oh! How a man proposes says
a lot about his character.


00:33:28.470 --> 00:33:30.529
- Yes.
- Yes, it does.


00:33:30.572 --> 00:33:33.200
I actually would love
to hear the story, Andrew.


00:33:33.241 --> 00:33:34.367
Would you tell us?


00:33:34.409 --> 00:33:36.741
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:33:36.778 --> 00:33:38.643
You know what?


00:33:38.680 --> 00:33:42.673
Actually, Margaret loves
telling this story...


00:33:42.717 --> 00:33:45.277
so I'm just gonna let her
go ahead and do that.


00:33:45.320 --> 00:33:47.515
'Cause I think we
should just sit in rapture.


00:33:47.555 --> 00:33:50.854
Huh! Wow, OK.


00:33:50.892 --> 00:33:54.726
Wow, where to begin... this story.


00:33:54.762 --> 00:33:57.754
Well... um, wow.


00:33:57.799 --> 00:33:59.858
Mmm... yeah.


00:33:59.901 --> 00:34:04.770
OK, well, um, Andrew and I...


00:34:04.806 --> 00:34:07.570
Andrew and I were about to celebrate


00:34:07.609 --> 00:34:10.203
- our first anniversary together.
- Aw...


00:34:10.245 --> 00:34:13.078
And I knew that he'd been
itching to ask me to marry him.


00:34:13.114 --> 00:34:16.311
And he was scared.
Like a little tiny bird.


00:34:16.351 --> 00:34:18.751
So I started leaving him
little hints here and there...


00:34:18.786 --> 00:34:21.550
...because I knew he wouldn't
have the guts to ask, but...


00:34:21.589 --> 00:34:24.422
That's not exactly how it happened.


00:34:24.459 --> 00:34:25.949
- No? Hmm.
- No. No.


00:34:25.994 --> 00:34:28.554
I mean, I picked up on
all her little hints.


00:34:28.596 --> 00:34:30.621
This woman's about as subtle as a gun.


00:34:30.665 --> 00:34:32.895
Yeah.


00:34:32.934 --> 00:34:34.265
What I was worried about was


00:34:34.302 --> 00:34:36.167
that she might find this little box...


00:34:36.204 --> 00:34:39.230
Oh! The decoupage box that he made


00:34:39.274 --> 00:34:41.435
where he'd taken the time to cut out


00:34:41.476 --> 00:34:44.240
tiny, little pictures of himself. Yes.


00:34:44.279 --> 00:34:47.976
Just pasted all over the
box. Oh! So beautiful.


00:34:48.016 --> 00:34:50.450
So I opened that beautiful,
little decoupage


00:34:50.485 --> 00:34:54.353
and out fluttered these tiny,
little hand-cut heart confettis.


00:34:54.389 --> 00:34:58.485
And once they cleared,
I looked down, and I saw...


00:34:58.526 --> 00:35:01.188
...the most beautiful, big...


00:35:01.229 --> 00:35:02.753
...fat nothing.


00:35:02.797 --> 00:35:04.162
No ring.


00:35:04.199 --> 00:35:05.791
- No ring?
- What?


00:35:05.833 --> 00:35:08.825
No. But inside that box...


00:35:08.870 --> 00:35:10.531
...underneath all that crap...


00:35:10.572 --> 00:35:12.836
...there was a little
handwritten note...


00:35:12.874 --> 00:35:16.401
with the address to
a hotel, date, and time.


00:35:16.444 --> 00:35:18.139
Real Humphrey Bogart-type stuff.


00:35:18.179 --> 00:35:19.544
Yeah.


00:35:19.581 --> 00:35:21.412
Masculine.


00:35:21.449 --> 00:35:23.314
Anyway, naturally, Margaret thought...


00:35:23.351 --> 00:35:24.909
I thought he was seeing someone else.


00:35:24.953 --> 00:35:27.080
It was a terrible time for me,


00:35:27.121 --> 00:35:29.487
but I went to that hotel anyway.


00:35:29.524 --> 00:35:31.617
I went there and I pounded on the door,


00:35:31.659 --> 00:35:33.490
but the door was already unlocked.


00:35:33.528 --> 00:35:37.396
And as swung open that
door, there he was...


00:35:37.432 --> 00:35:38.956
- Standing.
- Kneeling.


00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:40.558
- Like a man.
- On a bed of rose petals,


00:35:40.602 --> 00:35:44.060
in a tuxedo. Your son. Your son.


00:35:44.105 --> 00:35:47.666
And he was choking back
soft, soft sobs.


00:35:47.709 --> 00:35:50.974
And when he held back the tears
and finally caught his breath,


00:35:51.012 --> 00:35:52.070
he said to me...


00:35:52.113 --> 00:35:53.171
"Margaret, will you marry me?"


00:35:53.214 --> 00:35:56.547
And she said, "Yep."
The end. Who's hungry?


00:35:58.920 --> 00:36:01.582
That is quite a story.


00:36:01.623 --> 00:36:03.523
- Oh, Andy!
- Gorgeous.


00:36:03.558 --> 00:36:05.992
You are so sensitive.


00:36:06.794 --> 00:36:09.786
Hand-cut confetti?


00:36:09.831 --> 00:36:12.664
Hey! Let's see a kiss
from you two cuties.


00:36:12.700 --> 00:36:13.792
Give her a kiss!


00:36:13.835 --> 00:36:15.894
- No. Come on.
- Oh, yeah.


00:36:15.937 --> 00:36:16.961
Come on!


00:36:17.005 --> 00:36:18.563
OK, all right.


00:36:18.606 --> 00:36:20.471
OK. Here we go. Ready?


00:36:22.110 --> 00:36:26.376
What is this? Kiss her on
the mouth like you mean it.


00:36:26.414 --> 00:36:30.009
- Kiss her. Kiss her!
- Kiss her!


00:36:30.051 --> 00:36:33.953
Kiss her! Kiss her!
Kiss her! Kiss her!


00:36:33.988 --> 00:36:35.615
OK!


00:36:36.791 --> 00:36:37.849
- OK. All right.
- OK.


00:36:37.892 --> 00:36:40.053
- Here we go.
- Mmm-hmm. OK.


00:36:41.763 --> 00:36:43.560
Oh!


00:36:43.598 --> 00:36:46.226
Andy! Give her a real kiss!


00:36:46.267 --> 00:36:48.929
- Gammy.
- A real one!


00:36:48.970 --> 00:36:50.494
- Yeah.
- You can do it!


00:36:50.538 --> 00:36:52.199
Why don't we just do it?
Let's just do it really fast.


00:36:53.207 --> 00:36:55.801
Mmmm.


00:36:55.843 --> 00:36:58.778
- Mmm.
- Mmm-hmm. Mmm-hmm.


00:36:58.813 --> 00:37:00.974
- OK.
- Mmm.


00:37:09.691 --> 00:37:10.817
Hmm.


00:37:12.560 --> 00:37:14.824
I'm so happy for you two!


00:37:14.862 --> 00:37:18.229
So happy! So happy!


00:37:18.266 --> 00:37:20.131
Let's get the champagne!


00:37:21.069 --> 00:37:23.003
So here we are.


00:37:24.839 --> 00:37:26.568
This is your bedroom.


00:37:27.809 --> 00:37:33.770
Wow. Wow, this is, um...
beautiful. And the view.


00:37:33.815 --> 00:37:35.612
And here's the bed.


00:37:35.650 --> 00:37:38.448
Wow! Exquisite bed. Exquisite.


00:37:38.486 --> 00:37:41.455
So... where is Andrew's room?


00:37:41.489 --> 00:37:43.423
Oh, sweetie, we're not
under any illusions


00:37:43.458 --> 00:37:46.325
that you two don't
sleep in the same bed.


00:37:46.361 --> 00:37:48.625
He'll sleep
in here with you.


00:37:48.663 --> 00:37:51.029
Oh, great, 'cause we love to snuggle.


00:37:51.065 --> 00:37:52.999
- Don't we, honey.
- We're huge snugglers.


00:37:53.034 --> 00:37:55.264
Oh, my God. What is it?


00:37:55.303 --> 00:37:59.205
- Calm down, Kevin.
- Whoa! You are cute.


00:37:59.240 --> 00:38:00.832
Who is this?


00:38:00.875 --> 00:38:04.470
- That's Kevin. I'm sorry, Margaret.
- So cute.


00:38:04.512 --> 00:38:06.571
We just rescued him from the pound,


00:38:06.614 --> 00:38:08.605
and he's still in training. Sorry.


00:38:08.649 --> 00:38:10.617
Just be sure you don't
let him outside,


00:38:10.651 --> 00:38:12.448
or the eagles will snatch him.


00:38:12.487 --> 00:38:14.352
No, don't you listen to her.


00:38:14.389 --> 00:38:16.186
She's just pulling
your leg, isn't she?


00:38:16.224 --> 00:38:19.557
By the way, there are extra
towels and linens and things


00:38:19.594 --> 00:38:20.652
in here if you need them.


00:38:20.695 --> 00:38:22.526
And if you
get chilly tonight...


00:38:22.563 --> 00:38:24.224
...use this.


00:38:24.265 --> 00:38:25.994
It has special powers.


00:38:26.033 --> 00:38:29.025
Oh, what kind of special powers?


00:38:29.070 --> 00:38:30.697
I call it the Baby Maker.


00:38:30.738 --> 00:38:32.831
OK, well. Then I guess we...


00:38:32.874 --> 00:38:34.398
...gonna be super careful with that one.


00:38:34.442 --> 00:38:36.569
- Yeah, I'm just gonna...
- Don't throw it on the bed.


00:38:36.611 --> 00:38:38.579
We'd better turn in.
It's been quite an evening.


00:38:38.613 --> 00:38:40.342
So good night, everybody.


00:38:40.381 --> 00:38:41.678
- Good night.
- Good night.


00:38:41.716 --> 00:38:44.708
- Good night.
- Good night, Gammy.


00:38:46.254 --> 00:38:47.915
- Good night.
- Good night.


00:38:50.591 --> 00:38:52.650
- Good night.
- Good night, Gammy.


00:38:52.693 --> 00:38:54.126
Thank you so much. Sweet dreams.


00:38:54.162 --> 00:38:55.857
- Bye-bye, now.
- Bye.


00:38:59.033 --> 00:39:01.968
So, uh... you haven't
been home in a while.


00:39:02.003 --> 00:39:05.302
I haven't had a lot of vacation
time the last three years.


00:39:05.339 --> 00:39:07.534
Stop complaining.


00:39:09.944 --> 00:39:13.072
Um... Don't look, OK?


00:39:13.948 --> 00:39:15.210
OK.


00:39:16.451 --> 00:39:17.679
Are your eyes closed?


00:39:17.718 --> 00:39:19.015
Completely.


00:39:19.053 --> 00:39:22.420
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I'm sure.


00:39:31.065 --> 00:39:34.762
Those are the pajamas you
decided to bring to Alaska.


00:39:34.802 --> 00:39:38.260
Yes, because I was supposed
to be in a hotel alone.


00:39:38.306 --> 00:39:41.298
- Remember?
- Can we just go to sleep?


00:39:41.342 --> 00:39:43.401
- Fine.
- Great.


00:40:13.107 --> 00:40:15.302
Well.


00:40:15.343 --> 00:40:16.605
Looks like I won't be
getting much sleep


00:40:16.644 --> 00:40:19.169
with the sun streaming in.


00:40:25.553 --> 00:40:27.043
Thank you.


00:40:48.309 --> 00:40:50.209
Andrew. Phone.


00:40:50.745 --> 00:40:53.714
Andrew!


00:40:53.748 --> 00:40:56.148
Crap. Andrew, Andrew, phone.


00:40:56.183 --> 00:40:57.548
Andrew!


00:40:57.585 --> 00:40:59.519
Yeah... right.


00:41:03.157 --> 00:41:06.684
- Andrew, where is it?
- Purse, side pocket.


00:41:11.632 --> 00:41:15.295
Hello. Hello? Hello.


00:41:15.336 --> 00:41:17.201
Frank! Frank, darling.


00:41:17.238 --> 00:41:18.296
Darling, Frank.


00:41:18.339 --> 00:41:20.637
Are you there? Hello? Hello? Oh, crap.


00:41:20.675 --> 00:41:24.133
I have horrible service, Frank.
Give me just one minute.


00:41:24.178 --> 00:41:25.941
Oh, my God! Margaret!


00:41:25.980 --> 00:41:28.540
One... one minute.
Frank, hold on just a second.


00:41:28.583 --> 00:41:29.607
Frank, hold on. No, no, no, no.


00:41:30.785 --> 00:41:33.515
Frank. Frank, I'm sorry you feel


00:41:33.554 --> 00:41:36.216
I pressured you into doing Oprah, but...


00:41:36.257 --> 00:41:39.715
Of course I want you
to be happy. Yes, yes.


00:41:39.760 --> 00:41:45.596
Frank. Frank. Frank, darling.
Frank? It's going to be fine.


00:41:45.633 --> 00:41:47.760
I can just call them and I can cancel.


00:41:52.406 --> 00:41:54.874
You are...
you are so right, Frank.


00:41:54.909 --> 00:41:57.036
Yes, Frank, of course
I'm listening to you.


00:41:57.078 --> 00:41:58.739
Yeah... yes.


00:41:58.779 --> 00:42:00.371
I love listening to you, Frank.


00:42:00.414 --> 00:42:03.975
Shh! Sit. Sit.


00:42:05.319 --> 00:42:06.445
No, not you, Frank.


00:42:06.487 --> 00:42:08.284
No, no.


00:42:08.322 --> 00:42:10.051
Frank, if I may get down to it, OK...


00:42:10.091 --> 00:42:13.618
I think it would be
a mistake to back out.


00:42:13.661 --> 00:42:16.858
Because, Frank, for so many years...


00:42:16.897 --> 00:42:20.355
...you have inspired me with your
beautiful words, and I feel that...


00:42:20.401 --> 00:42:22.028
Shh! Dog, I'm on the phone.


00:42:22.069 --> 00:42:24.970
I think it's time that the world
get to enjoy your words as well.


00:42:25.006 --> 00:42:26.530
They are just so rich


00:42:26.574 --> 00:42:27.700
with... passion...


00:42:27.742 --> 00:42:32.406
And I think that we
should all be privy to.


00:42:32.446 --> 00:42:34.141
Frank, I just, uh...


00:42:34.181 --> 00:42:35.773
I just, uh, want you
to be happy, Frank.


00:42:35.816 --> 00:42:38.307
Give me that dog!


00:42:38.352 --> 00:42:40.786
Frank, hold on a second.
Can you hold a second?


00:42:40.821 --> 00:42:41.845
Give me that dog!


00:42:43.557 --> 00:42:45.081
Come on! Come on, come on, come on.


00:42:45.126 --> 00:42:47.390
Come on! Come on! Oh, oh...


00:42:47.428 --> 00:42:49.953
Oh, oh! Oh, oh. OK! OK, gotcha.


00:42:49.997 --> 00:42:51.828
Frank, Frank.


00:42:51.866 --> 00:42:53.060
Frank? So sorry, so sorry.


00:42:53.100 --> 00:42:56.228
So sorry. I dropped the phone.
Now, listen, Frank.


00:42:56.270 --> 00:42:59.000
I don't want to sell you on anything,


00:42:59.040 --> 00:43:00.837
but this is your legacy, this book.


00:43:00.875 --> 00:43:02.274
And I think it's up to you to


00:43:02.309 --> 00:43:03.333
present your legacy to the world.


00:43:03.377 --> 00:43:06.574
And call me tomorrow with your decision.


00:43:06.614 --> 00:43:08.343
And my phone is on
all the time! OK, bye-bye.


00:43:08.382 --> 00:43:09.406
No! Wait!


00:43:10.151 --> 00:43:12.813
No! No! N-n-n... no. No


00:43:12.853 --> 00:43:14.377
Take the doggy. Look at the doggy.


00:43:14.422 --> 00:43:16.322
I need that phone. Take the dog.


00:43:16.357 --> 00:43:17.824
Take the dog. I need that phone!


00:43:17.858 --> 00:43:21.157
Here. Take the dog.
