01:14:26.892 --> 01:14:28.484
Um, OK. Will I, uh...


01:14:28.527 --> 01:14:30.757
...are these shoes OK
for what we're gonna do?


01:14:32.131 --> 01:14:34.065
I can't believe this is happening.


01:14:35.134 --> 01:14:37.694
My mother made this dress by hand.


01:14:37.736 --> 01:14:41.502
In this very shop. In 1929.


01:14:41.540 --> 01:14:44.532
It's funny how things
come back in style.


01:14:44.577 --> 01:14:46.568
Just... just
finishing up the buttons.


01:14:46.612 --> 01:14:48.341
Yeah, and don't worry about the fit


01:14:48.380 --> 01:14:51.406
because Annie is the best
tailor in southeast Alaska.


01:14:51.450 --> 01:14:52.474
Oh... Pssh.


01:14:54.887 --> 01:14:56.411
Wow, incredible.


01:14:56.455 --> 01:14:59.015
Maybe a tad loose in certain
areas, but otherwise...


01:14:59.058 --> 01:15:02.789
Oh, sorry. I'm a bit
chesty to begin with


01:15:02.828 --> 01:15:05.524
and I happened to be
knocked up when I wore this.


01:15:05.564 --> 01:15:06.895
Oh.


01:15:06.932 --> 01:15:10.231
Oh, let's see if we can find your boobs.


01:15:12.304 --> 01:15:15.398
- They're in there somewhere.
- Yes. Yes, they are.


01:15:15.441 --> 01:15:17.272
This is like an Easter egg hunt.


01:15:18.444 --> 01:15:20.935
Maybe they shrunk up
in the cold Alaskan air.


01:15:23.916 --> 01:15:27.818
- Oh! There they are.
- That... yes. That would be...


01:15:27.853 --> 01:15:31.380
- There, let's see.
- I was thinking, if you'd like,


01:15:31.423 --> 01:15:36.156
maybe we could head down your
way for the holidays this year.


01:15:36.195 --> 01:15:38.390
Oh, that would, uh...
that would be nice.


01:15:38.430 --> 01:15:42.924
That'd be nice. Or maybe
we could come to you, too.


01:15:42.968 --> 01:15:46.699
- Well, that would be lovely.
- Mmm-hmm.


01:15:46.739 --> 01:15:48.900
I would like that very much.


01:15:48.941 --> 01:15:51.739
Oh, Grace, for God's sake.
We've got work to do.


01:15:51.777 --> 01:15:54.575
- I know. I'm sorry.
- Go make yourself a cup of tea.


01:15:54.613 --> 01:15:57.446
I'll finish this. Go.


01:15:57.483 --> 01:16:03.422
Now, let's make this
absolute perfection.


01:16:05.624 --> 01:16:11.119
Now, just one special touch
and you're ready.


01:16:14.867 --> 01:16:19.668
It's been in the family
for more than 150 years.


01:16:19.705 --> 01:16:21.673
Annie, it's beautiful,
but I don't really think...


01:16:21.707 --> 01:16:24.369
- Shh. I'm not finished.
- Oh, sorry.


01:16:24.410 --> 01:16:27.902
My great-grandfather gave it
to my great-grandmother


01:16:27.946 --> 01:16:30.107
when they got married.


01:16:30.149 --> 01:16:32.208
They were quite a scandal, you know.


01:16:32.251 --> 01:16:36.210
He was Russian and she
was Tlingit, and back then


01:16:36.255 --> 01:16:39.053
you had to get approval
from every member of the tribe


01:16:39.091 --> 01:16:40.422
before you got married.


01:16:40.459 --> 01:16:42.017
Almost broke them up.


01:16:42.061 --> 01:16:44.996
Well... how did they stay together then?


01:16:45.030 --> 01:16:47.726
She was a lot like you. Tough.


01:16:47.766 --> 01:16:50.701
Wouldn't take "no" for an answer.


01:16:50.736 --> 01:16:54.604
She was good for him.


01:16:54.640 --> 01:16:56.403
I want you to have it.


01:16:56.442 --> 01:16:59.934
- I can't. Can't take this.
- I don't want to hear it.


01:16:59.978 --> 01:17:03.607
Grandmothers love to give
their stuff to their grandchildren.


01:17:03.649 --> 01:17:06.379
It makes us feel like we'll
still be part of your lives


01:17:06.418 --> 01:17:07.817
even after we're gone.


01:17:07.853 --> 01:17:10.048
Take it.


01:17:15.360 --> 01:17:18.727
Are... are you all right, dear?


01:17:20.065 --> 01:17:22.727
I, uh...


01:17:24.269 --> 01:17:27.204
Uh... Well, I, um...


01:17:29.374 --> 01:17:35.108
I, uh... I just, uh, I just wanted to...


01:17:35.147 --> 01:17:37.911
make sure there was enough time
to get all the sewing done.


01:17:37.950 --> 01:17:40.919
Don't you worry about that.


01:17:40.953 --> 01:17:43.421
- You're gonna be beautiful.
- OK.


01:17:43.455 --> 01:17:47.050
- Now let's get you out of those pins.
- OK.


01:18:10.182 --> 01:18:11.308
All right.


01:18:16.388 --> 01:18:20.825
This is untied. Hop on in.


01:18:23.195 --> 01:18:25.595
Hey, hey, hey. Hey! Hey, hey, hey, hey!


01:18:26.298 --> 01:18:27.697
Whoa! What...


01:18:27.733 --> 01:18:29.291
Mind telling me what the hell's wrong?


01:18:29.334 --> 01:18:31.029
I just needed to get
away from everybody.


01:18:31.069 --> 01:18:33.094
- What's wrong?
- Nothing! Just stop talking, please!


01:18:41.547 --> 01:18:45.108
Would you mind telling me
what's happening now?


01:18:45.150 --> 01:18:46.617
Margaret.


01:18:49.254 --> 01:18:51.779
- Margaret!
- I forgot, OK?


01:18:51.824 --> 01:18:53.018
You forgot what?


01:18:53.058 --> 01:18:55.618
I forgot what it was
like to have a family!


01:18:55.661 --> 01:18:58.027
I've been on my own since I was 16


01:18:58.063 --> 01:19:00.998
and I forgot what it felt
like to have people love you


01:19:01.033 --> 01:19:03.297
and make you breakfast and say, "Hey!


01:19:03.335 --> 01:19:04.927
We'd love to come down
for the holidays."


01:19:04.970 --> 01:19:08.462
And I say, "Well, why don't we
come up and see you instead?"


01:19:08.507 --> 01:19:10.998
And give you necklaces!
And you have all that here,


01:19:11.043 --> 01:19:13.705
and you have Gertrude, and
I'm... I'm just screwing it up!


01:19:13.745 --> 01:19:15.975
You're not screwing it up!
I agreed to this!


01:19:16.014 --> 01:19:17.072
You were there, remember?


01:19:17.115 --> 01:19:18.673
Your family loves you. Do you know that?


01:19:18.717 --> 01:19:20.275
- I know that! Yes!
- You know that?


01:19:20.319 --> 01:19:21.980
And you're still willing
to put them through this?


01:19:22.020 --> 01:19:23.044
They're not gonna find out!


01:19:23.088 --> 01:19:24.385
How do you know they won't find out?


01:19:24.423 --> 01:19:25.754
Because you said so yourself.


01:19:25.791 --> 01:19:27.759
- I know, but what if your mother...
- You said so yourself!


01:19:27.793 --> 01:19:28.987
Oh, my God, if your mother found out...


01:19:29.027 --> 01:19:31.052
Whoa! Whoa!


01:19:31.096 --> 01:19:32.723
- Oh, my God! What if Gammy finds out?
- The boat is moving!


01:19:32.764 --> 01:19:34.197
If Gammy finds out, she's
gonna have a heart attack!


01:19:34.233 --> 01:19:36.167
Stop! It's gonna be fine!


01:19:36.201 --> 01:19:38.431
- She's gonna have a heart attack!
- Will you calm down! Hold on!


01:19:39.371 --> 01:19:40.895
Whoa, whoa. Whoa!


01:19:40.939 --> 01:19:44.568
Whoa! I don't think
that hijacking a boat


01:19:44.610 --> 01:19:48.205
is a proper way to
express your frustration!


01:19:48.247 --> 01:19:49.612
Now... Oh, great.


01:19:49.648 --> 01:19:51.980
Now you decide to shut up! Margaret?


01:19:52.017 --> 01:19:54.076
- Andrew!
- Margaret?


01:19:54.119 --> 01:19:56.781
- Andrew!
- Margaret!


01:20:00.592 --> 01:20:01.650
I can't swim!


01:20:01.693 --> 01:20:03.217
Margaret!


01:20:03.262 --> 01:20:04.524
To the buoy!


01:20:04.563 --> 01:20:07.031
- What?
- To the buoy!


01:20:07.933 --> 01:20:08.957
OK.


01:20:22.247 --> 01:20:24.613
All right, come on! Give me your hand!


01:20:24.650 --> 01:20:27.118
Hey! Give me your hand!


01:20:27.152 --> 01:20:29.848
Margaret! Give me...


01:20:29.888 --> 01:20:31.412
Come on, give me your hand!


01:20:31.456 --> 01:20:32.946
Come on, come on. I got you. I got you.


01:20:33.992 --> 01:20:35.482
I got you.


01:20:36.728 --> 01:20:39.128
Come on.


01:20:39.164 --> 01:20:40.995
What the hell
were you thinking?


01:20:41.033 --> 01:20:42.694
Could've gotten yourself killed.


01:20:42.734 --> 01:20:46.135
You turned the boat and
made me fall in, you jackass.


01:20:46.171 --> 01:20:48.196
You let go of the steering wheel, Ahab.


01:20:48.240 --> 01:20:50.868
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.


01:20:50.909 --> 01:20:54.208
All right, come here.
You've got to get warm. Come on.


01:20:54.246 --> 01:20:58.808
Come on. It's OK.


01:20:58.850 --> 01:21:00.010
That's OK.


01:21:03.422 --> 01:21:04.650
It's OK.


01:21:36.722 --> 01:21:38.212
I want to talk to both of you.


01:21:51.303 --> 01:21:53.931
Your mother is never to
hear about any of this.


01:22:06.251 --> 01:22:08.242
Told you I'd check up on you.


01:22:09.755 --> 01:22:10.983
What did you do?


01:22:11.023 --> 01:22:12.923
I got a phone call from
Mr. Gilbertson here,


01:22:12.958 --> 01:22:15.222
who told me that if you were lying,


01:22:15.260 --> 01:22:17.490
and he strongly believes that you are,


01:22:17.529 --> 01:22:19.053
he would send you to prison.


01:22:19.097 --> 01:22:21.190
So I flew him up here.


01:22:21.233 --> 01:22:23.258
- Dad.
- Luckily for you,


01:22:23.301 --> 01:22:26.327
your father negotiated
a deal on your behalf.


01:22:26.371 --> 01:22:29.602
Now, this offer's
gonna last for 20 seconds,


01:22:29.641 --> 01:22:31.370
so listen closely.


01:22:31.410 --> 01:22:32.502
You're gonna make a statement


01:22:32.544 --> 01:22:34.205
admitting this marriage is a sham...


01:22:34.246 --> 01:22:35.543
...or you're gonna go to prison.


01:22:35.580 --> 01:22:37.810
You tell the truth, you're off the hook,


01:22:37.849 --> 01:22:40.613
and she is going to go back to Canada.


01:22:46.024 --> 01:22:48.822
Ah, well. Take the deal.


01:22:48.860 --> 01:22:53.263
- I don't think so.
- Don't be stupid, Andrew.


01:22:53.298 --> 01:22:55.095
You want a statement?
Here's your statement.


01:22:55.133 --> 01:22:56.794
I've been working for
Margaret Tate for three years.


01:22:56.835 --> 01:22:59.133
Six months ago we started
dating, we fell in love.


01:22:59.171 --> 01:23:01.036
I asked her to marry me, she said "yes."


01:23:01.073 --> 01:23:03.268
I'll see you at the wedding.


01:23:13.952 --> 01:23:15.544
Well, you know.


01:23:36.875 --> 01:23:40.834
So...


01:23:40.879 --> 01:23:43.541
...you sure about this?


01:23:43.582 --> 01:23:45.140
Not really.


01:23:48.854 --> 01:23:51.687
I mean, I am very appreciative
of what you've done,


01:23:51.723 --> 01:23:52.747
but I think that...


01:23:52.791 --> 01:23:53.985
You'd do the same for me.


01:23:54.025 --> 01:23:55.652
Right?


01:23:57.062 --> 01:23:59.394
Hope everyone is decent.


01:23:59.431 --> 01:24:00.921
You need to come with me.


01:24:00.966 --> 01:24:02.661
Now, tomorrow
is your wedding day.


01:24:02.701 --> 01:24:04.362
You have to give the
Baby Maker a rest tonight.


01:24:04.402 --> 01:24:06.165
It's tradition.


01:24:06.204 --> 01:24:08.195
- Give your bride a kiss good night.
- We're not gonna...


01:24:08.240 --> 01:24:09.468
...use the Baby Maker.


01:24:09.508 --> 01:24:11.237
You've got your whole
lives to be together.


01:24:11.276 --> 01:24:14.074
- OK.
- Now, come on. Come on.


01:24:21.386 --> 01:24:22.580
If I don't go with her,
she's just gonna...


01:24:22.621 --> 01:24:26.523
- Come right back.
- Yeah.


01:24:33.498 --> 01:24:34.863
See you in the morning?


01:24:35.934 --> 01:24:37.333
Yeah.


01:25:40.365 --> 01:25:41.457
Hey, Gammy.


01:25:43.268 --> 01:25:45.031
- Thanks, Gammy.
- Oh.


01:26:54.706 --> 01:26:56.196
Everyone, please be seated.


01:27:02.180 --> 01:27:03.204
Ramone.


01:27:07.152 --> 01:27:11.885
We are gathered here
today to give thanks...


01:27:12.857 --> 01:27:15.485
...and to celebrate...


01:27:15.527 --> 01:27:18.087
...one of life's greatest moments.


01:27:18.129 --> 01:27:19.960
To give recognition


01:27:19.998 --> 01:27:24.765
to the beauty, honesty,
and unselfish ways


01:27:24.803 --> 01:27:27.601
of Andrew and Margaret's true love


01:27:27.639 --> 01:27:30.107
in front of family and friends.


01:27:30.141 --> 01:27:33.042
For it is their family and friends


01:27:33.078 --> 01:27:37.378
who taught Andrew and Margaret to love.


01:27:37.415 --> 01:27:42.182
So it is only right that
family and friends are all...


01:27:45.690 --> 01:27:47.920
<i>Mi amor.</i> Do you have a question?


01:27:48.760 --> 01:27:50.728
Uh, no...


01:27:50.762 --> 01:27:52.252
Your hand is up.


01:27:55.834 --> 01:27:58.860
Oh, it, it's, uh, not a question,


01:27:58.903 --> 01:28:01.167
but I do have something I need to say.


01:28:01.206 --> 01:28:05.142
- Margaret.
- Can it wait till after?


01:28:05.176 --> 01:28:09.704
Uh... No. No.


01:28:21.092 --> 01:28:24.994
- Hi there.
- Hi.


01:28:25.029 --> 01:28:27.190
Thank you all so much for coming out.


01:28:27.232 --> 01:28:30.395
I, uh... have
a bit of an announcement


01:28:30.435 --> 01:28:32.562
to make about the wedding.


01:28:32.604 --> 01:28:35.903
- A confession, actually.
- What are you doing?


01:28:35.940 --> 01:28:39.501
Uh... I'm a Canadian. Yes, Canadian.


01:28:39.544 --> 01:28:43.708
With an expired visa
who was about to be deported.


01:28:43.748 --> 01:28:45.409
And because I didn't want to leave


01:28:45.450 --> 01:28:47.680
this wonderful country of yours,


01:28:47.719 --> 01:28:50.654
I forced Andrew here to marry me.


01:28:50.688 --> 01:28:52.121
Margaret, stop it.


01:28:52.157 --> 01:28:56.025
See, Andrew has always had
this extraordinary work ethic.


01:28:57.495 --> 01:28:59.156
Something I think he learned from you.


01:29:00.465 --> 01:29:02.524
And for three years I
watched him work harder


01:29:02.567 --> 01:29:04.535
than anyone else at our company.


01:29:04.569 --> 01:29:07.834
And I knew that if I threatened
to destroy his career...


01:29:07.872 --> 01:29:11.069
...he would, he would do
just about anything.


01:29:14.646 --> 01:29:18.673
So I blackmailed him to
come up here and to lie to you.


01:29:20.819 --> 01:29:23.845
All of you.


01:29:23.888 --> 01:29:26.618
And I thought it would
be easy to watch him do it.


01:29:28.760 --> 01:29:30.318
But it wasn't.


01:29:33.198 --> 01:29:35.359
Turns out it's not easy
to ruin someone's life


01:29:35.400 --> 01:29:38.028
once you find out
how wonderful they are.


01:29:44.275 --> 01:29:46.300
You have a beautiful family.


01:29:48.146 --> 01:29:50.273
Don't let this
come between you.


01:29:53.318 --> 01:29:55.616
This was my fault.


01:29:55.653 --> 01:29:57.484
Margaret...


01:29:57.522 --> 01:29:59.422
Andrew, this was a business deal,


01:29:59.457 --> 01:30:03.484
and you held up your end,
but now the deal is off.


01:30:04.762 --> 01:30:06.059
I'm sorry.


01:30:07.966 --> 01:30:09.194
And, you, meet me at the dock.


01:30:09.234 --> 01:30:11.031
You're giving me a ride to the airport.


01:30:27.852 --> 01:30:30.343
- What were you thinking?
- I don't, I don't know.


01:30:30.388 --> 01:30:31.980
Andrew, you lied to us.


01:30:32.023 --> 01:30:33.422
Let me get my head on straight, OK?


01:30:33.458 --> 01:30:34.857
I'll explain everything later.


01:30:34.893 --> 01:30:37.225
I'm sorry.


01:31:14.632 --> 01:31:17.499
<i> You were right.</i>
<i>This book is special.</i>


01:31:17.535 --> 01:31:19.162
<i>I lied because I knew publishing meant</i>


01:31:19.203 --> 01:31:20.465
<i>I'd lose you as an assistant</i>


01:31:20.505 --> 01:31:22.735
<i>but... you have an extraordinary eye,</i>


01:31:22.774 --> 01:31:25.800
<i>and I'll make sure we</i>
<i>buy this before I leave.</i>


01:31:25.843 --> 01:31:29.973
<i>Have an amazing life.</i>
<i>You deserve it. Margaret.</i>


01:31:32.216 --> 01:31:35.447
Well, that was, uh... crazy.


01:31:36.854 --> 01:31:39.288
You know, people are gonna be
talking about this forever.


01:31:41.192 --> 01:31:42.819
Yeah. Yeah.


01:31:44.529 --> 01:31:45.655
Are you OK?


01:31:46.898 --> 01:31:49.765
Yeah. No. Uh...


01:31:51.936 --> 01:31:55.804
I just feel... You know
what the problem is?


01:31:55.840 --> 01:31:59.037
The problem is that this woman...


01:31:59.077 --> 01:32:02.604
...is a gigantic pain in my ass.


01:32:02.647 --> 01:32:05.115
First there's the whole leaving
thing. I understand that.


01:32:05.149 --> 01:32:07.947
It's a sham wedding.
It's kind of stressful.


01:32:07.986 --> 01:32:11.012
But then she goes ahead
and she leaves this note.


01:32:11.055 --> 01:32:12.920
Because she doesn't have the decency...


01:32:12.957 --> 01:32:15.084
the humanity to do it to my face.


01:32:15.126 --> 01:32:20.223
Three years. Three years
I work with this... this terrorist.


01:32:20.264 --> 01:32:21.856
Never once has she had
a nice thing to say,


01:32:21.899 --> 01:32:23.764
and then she goes ahead
and she writes this crap!


01:32:23.801 --> 01:32:25.564
- Andrew.
- But none of that matters


01:32:25.603 --> 01:32:26.831
because we had a deal!


01:32:26.871 --> 01:32:31.069
- Andrew.
- Sorry. I'm sorry. I just...


01:32:31.109 --> 01:32:32.303
She just makes me a little crazy.


01:32:32.343 --> 01:32:35.779
Yeah. I can see that.


01:32:35.813 --> 01:32:39.874
So you're just gonna let her go?


01:32:53.164 --> 01:32:55.132
So, what now?


01:32:55.166 --> 01:32:58.135
Well... now that
you're leaving voluntarily,


01:32:58.169 --> 01:33:00.865
it all becomes very civilized.


01:33:00.905 --> 01:33:03.669
Once we land in New York,
you have 24 hours


01:33:03.708 --> 01:33:06.734
to head back to Canada.


01:33:14.118 --> 01:33:16.450
- Andrew, what's happening?
- I got to talk to her.


01:33:16.487 --> 01:33:17.715
- Why would you do that?
- Boys!


01:33:17.755 --> 01:33:18.779
This has nothing to do with you.


01:33:18.823 --> 01:33:19.847
Boys, stop it! Stop it!


01:33:19.891 --> 01:33:21.381
I'm not gonna let you do this.


01:33:21.426 --> 01:33:22.893
I'm not asking
your permission here.


01:33:22.927 --> 01:33:26.124
Annie! Joe! Joe!


01:33:26.164 --> 01:33:29.361
Annie! Joe!


01:33:29.400 --> 01:33:32.392
I think I'm having a heart attack.


01:33:32.437 --> 01:33:33.870
- Easy. Easy.
- Somebody get a doctor!


01:33:33.905 --> 01:33:35.736
- Easy, easy.
- Get a doctor!


01:33:39.777 --> 01:33:40.869
I got it.


01:34:09.407 --> 01:34:11.136
Andrew.


01:34:13.711 --> 01:34:17.112
You two need to stop fighting.


01:34:17.148 --> 01:34:19.810
You'll never see eye to eye.


01:34:21.119 --> 01:34:24.748
But you're family.


01:34:28.092 --> 01:34:33.029
Promise me you'll stand by Andrew.


01:34:33.064 --> 01:34:35.931
Even if... if you don't agree with him.


01:34:38.302 --> 01:34:39.667
I promise.


01:34:41.606 --> 01:34:44.040
Andrew.


01:34:44.075 --> 01:34:50.036
Promise me you'll work harder
to be a part of this family.


01:34:50.081 --> 01:34:52.106
I will.


01:34:54.752 --> 01:34:57.084
I will, Gammy.


01:34:57.121 --> 01:35:02.753
Well, then, the spirits can take me.


01:35:02.794 --> 01:35:04.557
Oh, Annie.


01:35:11.302 --> 01:35:12.963
Gammy?


01:35:19.443 --> 01:35:21.172
I guess they're not ready for me.


01:35:22.413 --> 01:35:24.244
I'm feeling much better, sonny.


01:35:24.282 --> 01:35:26.182
No need to take us
to the hospital.


01:35:26.217 --> 01:35:28.014
Take us to the airport, please.


01:35:28.052 --> 01:35:29.883
Mom, what? Are you faking
the heart attack?


01:35:29.921 --> 01:35:31.354
Oh, come on!


01:35:31.389 --> 01:35:33.220
Well, it was the only
way I could get you two


01:35:33.257 --> 01:35:35.657
to shut up and get us to the airport!


01:35:35.693 --> 01:35:37.752
Ma'am, we're not authorized
to take you to the airport.


01:35:37.795 --> 01:35:40.764
Larry Ferris, don't
make me call your mother.


01:35:40.798 --> 01:35:42.959
You got it.


01:35:44.535 --> 01:35:46.833
You scared the hell out of me.


01:35:51.943 --> 01:35:56.004
Yep. You should've
given up back in New York.


01:35:56.047 --> 01:35:59.278
See, I'm like Eliot Ness.


01:35:59.317 --> 01:36:02.411
I always get my man.


01:36:02.453 --> 01:36:05.479
I'm that good.


01:36:05.523 --> 01:36:07.650
Flight 1601, as soon
as you're in position,


01:36:07.692 --> 01:36:08.989
you're cleared for takeoff.


01:36:09.026 --> 01:36:10.152
<i> Roger that, Chuck.</i>


01:36:18.202 --> 01:36:20.102
OK. Come on, come on,
come on, come on.


01:36:26.310 --> 01:36:27.868
Tower. Talk to me.


01:36:27.912 --> 01:36:30.005
- Chuck! It's Drew Paxton.
- <i>Hey, dude.</i>


01:36:30.047 --> 01:36:33.039
Hey, uh... I have a little
favor I need from you, buddy...


01:36:33.084 --> 01:36:35.143
Margaret's on that plane. I got
to talk to her. Can you stop it?


01:36:35.186 --> 01:36:36.483
<i> Oh, yeah!</i>


01:36:36.520 --> 01:36:38.283
I heard about your lady bailin'.


01:36:38.322 --> 01:36:41.348
- Drag-ola.
- <i> Chuck! I need you</i>


01:36:41.392 --> 01:36:42.916
to stop the plane. Please.


01:36:42.960 --> 01:36:45.827
<i>I can't do that. </i>


01:36:45.863 --> 01:36:49.196
No, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no! Come on!


01:36:50.001 --> 01:36:51.400
Oh, no.


01:36:53.571 --> 01:36:55.266
No!


01:36:57.041 --> 01:36:58.941
- What's wrong?
- Margaret's on that plane.


01:36:58.976 --> 01:37:01.240
- And he didn't get to tell her.
- Tell her what?


01:37:01.279 --> 01:37:02.746
That he loves her.


01:37:02.780 --> 01:37:05.613
So she could tell him
that she loves him, too.


01:37:05.650 --> 01:37:06.810
OK, but how does he...


01:37:06.851 --> 01:37:08.216
If she didn't love him,
she wouldn't have left.


01:37:08.252 --> 01:37:09.742
Of course not.


01:37:09.787 --> 01:37:11.311
Am I the only one not getting this?


01:37:11.355 --> 01:37:15.223
- Oh, Joe!
- Chuck! Chuck! Look down.


01:37:15.259 --> 01:37:16.726
Oh! Oh. Look down.


01:37:16.761 --> 01:37:19.059
<i>Like... Oh, there you are!</i>


01:37:19.096 --> 01:37:21.223
<i>Sorry, man. There was</i>
<i>nothing I could do.</i>


01:37:23.234 --> 01:37:24.895
Thanks, Chuck.


01:37:27.972 --> 01:37:32.238
I'm sorry, son. I didn't
know how you felt about her.


01:37:37.448 --> 01:37:39.040
Honey, it's gonna be OK.


01:38:12.516 --> 01:38:13.983
Jordan?


01:38:32.303 --> 01:38:33.327
Jordan.


01:38:34.705 --> 01:38:36.172
Jordan!


01:38:36.207 --> 01:38:39.540
I need for you to send
the boxes in my office to...


01:38:39.577 --> 01:38:41.169
...to this address, please.


01:38:41.212 --> 01:38:45.546
This one right here.
This address right here. OK?


01:38:45.583 --> 01:38:48.143
- Can you do that?
- Uh, yes. Sure.


01:38:48.185 --> 01:38:50.050
- Good, all right. Thank you.
- Miss Tate.


01:38:50.087 --> 01:38:53.284
Yes. What? What?


01:38:55.159 --> 01:38:58.526
Hey.


01:38:59.897 --> 01:39:02.525
Andrew.


01:39:06.337 --> 01:39:08.965
Why are, why are you panting?


01:39:09.006 --> 01:39:11.167
Because I've been running.


01:39:11.208 --> 01:39:14.041
- Really. From Alaska?
- I need to talk to you.


01:39:14.078 --> 01:39:15.773
Yeah? Well, I don't have time to talk.


01:39:15.813 --> 01:39:18.213
I need to catch a 5:45 to Toronto.


01:39:18.249 --> 01:39:19.944
- Margaret.
- I need the boxes to go out today.


01:39:19.984 --> 01:39:21.042
I want to make sure everything is...


01:39:21.085 --> 01:39:23.178
Margaret! Stop talking!


01:39:27.291 --> 01:39:28.781
Gotta say something.


01:39:28.826 --> 01:39:30.521
- OK.
- This will just take a sec.


01:39:30.561 --> 01:39:32.461
Fine. What?


01:39:33.464 --> 01:39:38.197
Three days ago, I loathed you.


01:39:38.235 --> 01:39:40.430
I used to dream about you
getting hit by a cab.


01:39:40.471 --> 01:39:41.768
Or poisoned.


01:39:41.806 --> 01:39:45.401
- Oh, that's nice.
- I told you to stop talking.


01:39:45.443 --> 01:39:48.037
Then we had our little
adventure up in Alaska


01:39:48.079 --> 01:39:50.445
and things started to change.


01:39:50.481 --> 01:39:53.143
Things changed when we kissed.


01:39:55.119 --> 01:39:57.053
And when you told me about your tattoo.


01:39:59.690 --> 01:40:01.885
Even when you checked me
out when we were naked.


01:40:01.926 --> 01:40:03.291
Uh-huuuh.


01:40:03.327 --> 01:40:04.453
Naked?


01:40:04.495 --> 01:40:06.463
Well, I didn't see anything...


01:40:06.497 --> 01:40:07.862
Yeah, you did.


01:40:07.898 --> 01:40:12.164
But I didn't realize any of
this until I was standing alone.


01:40:12.203 --> 01:40:16.003
In a barn... wife-less.


01:40:16.040 --> 01:40:18.668
Now, you can imagine my disappointment


01:40:18.709 --> 01:40:20.176
when it suddenly dawned on me


01:40:20.211 --> 01:40:24.511
that the woman I love is about
to be kicked out of the country.


01:40:27.118 --> 01:40:28.949
So, Margaret.


01:40:31.188 --> 01:40:32.314
Marry me.


01:40:35.759 --> 01:40:38.250
Because I'd like to date you.


01:40:50.474 --> 01:40:53.807
Trust me. You don't really
want to be with me.


01:40:53.844 --> 01:40:55.573
Yes, I do.


01:40:57.214 --> 01:41:00.206
See, the thing is, there is a reason why


01:41:00.251 --> 01:41:02.845
I've been alone all this time.


01:41:02.887 --> 01:41:04.855
I'm comfortable that way.


01:41:04.889 --> 01:41:06.914
And I think it would
just be a lot easier


01:41:06.957 --> 01:41:12.987
if we forgot everything
that happened and I just left.


01:41:14.865 --> 01:41:16.457
You're right.


01:41:21.972 --> 01:41:24.566
That would be easier.


01:41:40.357 --> 01:41:43.815
- I'm scared.
- Me, too.


01:42:07.685 --> 01:42:10.620
Aren't you supposed to get down
on your knee or something?


01:42:10.654 --> 01:42:12.178
I'm gonna take that as a "yes."


01:42:12.223 --> 01:42:14.248
Oh, OK.


01:42:28.772 --> 01:42:31.707
Yeah! Show her
who's boss, Andrew!


01:42:39.817 --> 01:42:43.446
So, let me see
if I've got this right.


01:42:43.487 --> 01:42:45.921
You two are engaged again.


01:42:45.956 --> 01:42:47.514
- Yes.
- Yes.


01:42:47.558 --> 01:42:49.651
For real?


01:42:50.594 --> 01:42:51.754
- Yes.
- Yeah.


01:42:51.795 --> 01:42:52.853
You're sure you want to
go through with this?


01:42:52.896 --> 01:42:54.022
Because one wrong answer...


01:42:54.064 --> 01:42:57.261
I'm gonna take you down.


01:42:59.637 --> 01:43:02.333
- OK.
- OK.


01:43:03.974 --> 01:43:05.271
Let's do it.


01:43:14.718 --> 01:43:16.242
When did you
first start to date?


01:43:16.287 --> 01:43:18.152
Last week.


01:43:18.188 --> 01:43:21.419
- That going well?
- So far it's great. Thank you.


01:43:21.458 --> 01:43:22.948
What kind of
deodorant does Andrew use?


01:43:22.993 --> 01:43:24.551
Men's Speed Stick?


01:43:24.595 --> 01:43:27.894
What flavor? Musk? Alpine?


01:43:27.931 --> 01:43:29.228
Was it love at first sight?


01:43:29.266 --> 01:43:31.393
No.


01:43:31.435 --> 01:43:35.269
I loved her from the beginning.


01:43:35.306 --> 01:43:36.568
What side of the
bed does Margaret sleep on?


01:43:36.607 --> 01:43:38.336
She sleeps on the left.


01:43:38.375 --> 01:43:39.808
What side of the bed do you sleep on?


01:43:41.845 --> 01:43:46.179
Look, are they soul mates? Eeeh.


01:43:46.216 --> 01:43:48.844
Uh... Will they kill each other? No.


01:43:48.886 --> 01:43:50.012
Are you a good driver?


01:43:50.054 --> 01:43:52.648
Oh, excellent driver. Excellent.


01:43:56.427 --> 01:43:58.827
Oh.


01:43:58.862 --> 01:44:01.854
In my mind I see her
with someone perhaps...


01:44:01.899 --> 01:44:03.799
...more swarthy, darker.


01:44:03.834 --> 01:44:06.462
We don't use the word
"Margaret" around Kevin.


01:44:06.503 --> 01:44:10.803
He still hasn't warmed up to her.


01:44:10.841 --> 01:44:12.536
Margaret.


01:44:12.576 --> 01:44:14.567
Margaret.


01:44:14.611 --> 01:44:16.340
See? It's the damnedest thing.


01:44:16.380 --> 01:44:18.007
I have never farted in front of him.


01:44:18.048 --> 01:44:20.448
Nor will I ever fart in front of him.


01:44:20.484 --> 01:44:23.009
She farts in her sleep.


01:44:23.053 --> 01:44:24.953
Would you consider
Margaret a good dancer?


01:44:24.988 --> 01:44:28.219
You can tell by the way
she drinks her soda pop


01:44:28.258 --> 01:44:30.624
that she's a good dancer.


01:44:30.661 --> 01:44:31.889
Uh-huh. How, how...


01:44:31.929 --> 01:44:36.366
How is the soda pop
relevant to the dancing?


01:44:36.400 --> 01:44:38.061
I don't understand this.


01:44:38.102 --> 01:44:41.037
- I call him... puppy.
- Pumpkin.


01:44:41.071 --> 01:44:42.732
- Monkey.
- Daisy.


01:44:42.773 --> 01:44:44.968
- Kiddo.
- Uh... Bird.


01:44:45.008 --> 01:44:48.205
Sometimes I call him Rick.


01:44:48.245 --> 01:44:49.712
How do you spell "Ramone?"


01:44:49.747 --> 01:44:52.614
R-A-M-O-N-E.


01:44:52.649 --> 01:44:54.549
Could you do that
again in English, please?


01:44:54.585 --> 01:44:57.452
When you say, you know, the
position in the relationship...


01:44:57.488 --> 01:44:58.853
Top or bottom?


01:44:58.889 --> 01:45:01.858
You're asking me a question
about who's on top?


01:45:01.892 --> 01:45:03.621
You took an oath
when you walked in this office.


01:45:03.660 --> 01:45:06.128
I did not take an oath.
When did I take an oath?


01:45:06.163 --> 01:45:07.425
Laura should've
done that, but she didn't.


01:45:07.464 --> 01:45:09.329
- That's OK.
- Who's Laura?


01:45:09.366 --> 01:45:11.698
She's the girl behind you.
Don't look around.


01:45:11.735 --> 01:45:12.997
Which of
the following numbers


01:45:13.036 --> 01:45:15.834
- is not a prime?
- Seventeen.


01:45:15.873 --> 01:45:18.034
I'm sorry. Let me say the list, please.


01:45:18.075 --> 01:45:19.099
I'm sorry?


01:45:19.143 --> 01:45:20.405
He knew
your favorite color.


01:45:20.444 --> 01:45:22.071
- Blue?
- Wrong!


01:45:22.112 --> 01:45:23.636
- Red?
- No!


01:45:23.680 --> 01:45:25.204
Dark... Maybe like a hunter green?


01:45:25.249 --> 01:45:26.648
No. White.


01:45:26.683 --> 01:45:27.945
- White?
- OK, moving on.


01:45:27.985 --> 01:45:29.384
Favorite color is blue.


01:45:29.420 --> 01:45:33.322
What's her favorite color
when she's not at home?


01:45:33.357 --> 01:45:34.756
I don't know.


01:45:34.792 --> 01:45:36.555
Are you a citizen
of this country, Ramone?


01:45:36.593 --> 01:45:40.461
Yes, I'm a citizen!
Are you crazy?


01:45:42.499 --> 01:45:45.400
What relevance a ball in a net


01:45:45.436 --> 01:45:47.370
or a Fruit Roll-Up or a Pop-Tart


01:45:47.404 --> 01:45:49.964
has to do with my
relationship with Andrew?


01:45:50.007 --> 01:45:51.531
If you're
getting excited...


01:45:51.575 --> 01:45:54.703
Who are you engaged to?


01:45:54.745 --> 01:45:58.943
- Andrew.
- Very good. Got one right.


01:45:58.982 --> 01:46:00.142
Who are you engaged to?


01:46:00.184 --> 01:46:01.879
I'm engaged to Margaret Tate.


01:46:01.919 --> 01:46:07.380
And on the wedding day,
who will be next to you?


01:46:07.424 --> 01:46:09.722
I'm going to marry Margaret Tate.


01:46:09.760 --> 01:46:12.456
- Final answer?
- That work? Yeah, final answer.


01:46:12.496 --> 01:46:15.795
Is this a game show?
I don't understand what...


01:46:22.906 --> 01:46:24.373
That's a great song.


01:46:24.408 --> 01:46:26.137
That was beautiful.
That was really beautiful.


01:46:26.176 --> 01:46:27.837
Mama Cass.

